window.CHENHUA_SEARCH_INDEX = {"records": {"gu-kaizhi-admonitions-scroll-400": ["《女史箴图》 400 约380–400（唐摹本） 中国 顾恺之（传） 中国六朝绘画 面孔 人间 中国 绢本设色 维基共享资源 《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国人物画手卷之一，一般认为是唐代摹本，原作作者是顾恺之。画中以九个存留下来的场景描绘了张华《女史箴》里的十二段故事：冯女护驾熊袭、班女辞帝车，以及宫女梳妆或坐着聊天下棋。衣纹轻盈飘动，线条细腻连贯，就像蚕丝般柔顺。\n\n画中没有透视和阴影，但通过线条的节奏、人物间的距离以及空白处来组织叙事。这幅作品既是道德教材，也像是一幅宫廷女性生活的影像史。它在1900年义和团事件后流入英国，现在收藏于大英博物馆。", "admonitions of the instructress to the court ladies 400 约380–400（唐摹本） china 顾恺之（传） six dynasties painting faces human world china ink and colour on silk wikimedia commons admonitions of the instructress to the court ladies is among the earliest surviving chinese handscrolls of figure painting, generally regarded as a tang-dynasty copy after gu kaizhi. it illustrates twelve passages from zhang hua's admonitions in the form of nine surviving scenes: lady feng shielding the emperor from a bear, lady ban declining the imperial carriage, and court ladies at their toilet or seated in conversation. draperies lift and flow; lines are fine and unbroken, like silk spun by a silkworm.\n\nthere is no perspective and no shadow, yet rhythm of line, distance between figures and blank space organise the narrative. it is both a moral textbook and an image-history of palace women's lives. it entered britain after the boxer upheaval in 1900 and is now in the british museum."], "juran-buddhist-retreat-975": ["《溪山兰若图》 buddhist retreat by stream and mountains 975 960–85 中国 五代北宋 巨然 北宋山水 风景 天地 中国 绢本水墨 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 960–85，中国 五代北宋。巨然的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "buddhist retreat by stream and mountains 975 960–85 中国 五代北宋 巨然 northern song landscape landscape heaven and earth china 绢本水墨 cleveland museum of art 960–85, china. 巨然; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1959.348. this is a painting (绢本水墨)."], "fan-kuan-travelers-1025": ["《溪山行旅图》 1025 约1025 中国 范宽 北宋山水 风景 天地 中国 绢本水墨 维基共享资源 《溪山行旅图》是北宋山水画的巅峰之作。一座巨大的中央山峰向前凸出，山顶隐没在雾中；右侧有瀑布垂下，山脚下有一条小路，驮驴队和两个旅人正沿路前行。人物几乎看不见，被放在画面下方，以衬托山的高大。\n\n范宽用密集的“雨点”皴法堆砌岩石的重量，通过层层叠墨，让山体看起来仿佛真能挡住道路。他追求的不是风景如画的效果，而是那种山就在那里、沉重逼人的气势。", "travelers among mountains and streams 1025 约1025 china 范宽 northern song landscape landscape heaven and earth china ink on silk wikimedia commons travelers among mountains and streams is the summit of northern song landscape. a vast central peak presses forward, its summit lost in mist; a waterfall falls at the right, and at the foot a path carries a train of pack donkeys and two travelers. the figures are almost invisible, placed low in the picture to measure the mountain's height.\n\nfan kuan builds the weight of rock from dense \"raindrop\" texture strokes, layering ink until the mass feels like something that would actually block the road. he seeks not the picturesque but the pressure of a mountain that is simply there."], "zhang-zeduan-qingming-scroll-1100": ["《清明上河图》 1100 约1085–1145 中国 张择端 北宋风俗画 街巷 人间 中国 绢本设色 维基共享资源 《清明上河图》展示了北宋首都汴京在清明时节的全景。这幅卷从城外的柳树和运货队伍开始，经过汴河上的虹桥，进入城门和集市：船夫、挑夫、小贩、说书人、轿子、骆驼、酒馆、药铺——数百个人物，每个人都有动作，甚至桥边小贩的伞都画得栩栩如生。\n\n张择端画的不是宫廷，而是城市的运作：粮食运输、税收、消费、交通与娱乐。虹桥是高潮：一只大船正在降低桅杆以通过桥下，而桥上的人群喊叫观看。这既是一幅风俗画，也是一份十一世纪城市生活的社会记录。", "along the river during the qingming festival 1100 约1085–1145 china 张择端 northern song genre painting streets human world china ink and colour on silk wikimedia commons along the river during the qingming festival presents a panoramic view of the northern song capital bianjing at the qingming season. the scroll begins in willows and pack teams outside the city, passes the rainbow bridge over the bian river, and enters gates and markets: boatmen, porters, vendors, storytellers, sedan chairs, camels, taverns, pharmacies — hundreds of figures, each with an action, down to the parasols of bridge-side hawkers.\n\nzhang zeduan paints not the court but how a city works: grain transport, taxation, consumption, traffic and entertainment. the rainbow bridge is the climax: a large boat is lowering its mast to pass beneath while crowds on the bridge shout and watch. it is both a genre painting and a social record of eleventh-century urban life."], "wang-ximeng-thousand-li-1113": ["《千里江山图》 1113 1113 中国 王希孟 北宋青绿山水 风景 天地 中国 绢本设色 维基共享资源 《千里江山图》是北宋青绿山水的巅峰之作。王希孟画这幅画时才十八岁；画卷近十二米长，层层涂抹着蓝铜矿和孔雀石，山川、村落、桥梁和渔船在矿物色泽中徐徐展开。画面没有单一的焦点，视线沿着水面慢慢游走。\n\n青绿不是对自然的模仿，而是理想化的国土：蓝色闪耀，绿色透亮。它把“江山”变成一个可以游览和治理的空间，同时是绘画也是政治想象。", "a thousand li of rivers and mountains 1113 1113 china 王希孟 northern song blue-and-green landscape landscape heaven and earth china ink and colour on silk wikimedia commons a thousand li of rivers and mountains is the peak of northern song blue-and-green landscape. wang ximeng was only eighteen when he painted it; the scroll runs nearly twelve metres, layered with azurite and malachite so that mountains, rivers, villages, bridges and fishing boats unfold in mineral light. there is no single focus; the eye travels slowly along the water.\n\nthe blue-green is not an imitation of nature but an idealised country: blue that shines, green that is transparent. it turns \"rivers and mountains\" into a space that can be toured and governed, at once painting and political imagination."], "muqi-dragon-1260": ["《龙图》 dragon 1260 c. 1250–79 中国 南宋 牧溪（法常） 禅宗绘画 风景 天地 中国 绢本水墨 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1250–79，中国 南宋。牧溪（法常）的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "dragon 1260 c. 1250–79 中国 南宋 牧溪（法常） chan painting landscape heaven and earth china 绢本水墨 cleveland museum of art c. 1250–79, china. 牧溪（法常）; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1958.427.1. this is a painting (绢本水墨)."], "giotto-lamentation-1305": ["《哀悼基督》 1305 约1305 欧洲 乔托 早期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 湿壁画 维基共享资源 在帕多瓦的斯克罗维尼教堂，乔托把拜占庭的圣像变成了有重量、有呼吸的身体。玛丽靠近基督的脸，约翰张开双臂，抹大拉的玛利亚握着他的脚；一个斜斜的岩石台阶把目光引向死去的身体，把整个场景压在左下角。在天空中，天使在哭泣，他们的悲伤几乎可见。\n\n乔托把场景放在灰蓝色的岩石和土地上，而不是金色背景里，用体积感、空间深度和可识别的表情代替了象征性的秩序。衣服有了厚度，脸上有了阴影，悲伤也有了不同的层次。艺术史上通常把这一刻视为西方绘画从圣像走向自然的转折点。", "lamentation 1305 约1305 europe 乔托 early renaissance faces human world europe fresco wikimedia commons in the scrovegni chapel in padua, giotto turned the byzantine icon into bodies that weigh and breathe. mary bends close to christ's face, john throws his arms wide, mary magdalene holds the feet; a diagonal rock ledge drives the eye down to the dead figure and presses the whole group into the lower left corner. in the sky, angels weep, their grief almost visible.\n\ngiotto set the scene on grey-blue rock and earth rather than against a gold ground, replacing symbolic order with volume, spatial depth and recognisable expression. drapery acquires thickness, faces acquire shadow, and grief acquires different degrees. art history often treats this moment as the point where western painting turns from icon towards nature."], "duccio-maesta-1308": ["《圣母登宝座》（《马埃斯塔》） 1308 1308–1311 欧洲 杜乔·迪·博宁塞尼亚 早期文艺复兴 信仰 人间 欧洲 蛋彩与金箔（木板） 维基共享资源 《威严》是杜乔为锡耶纳大教堂创作的双面祭坛画的正面板，于1311年像圣物一样被抬过街道。圣母端坐在宝座上，怀抱基督儿童，周围环绕着圣人和天使；金色的背景将人群压缩到一个发光的平面上。杜乔并没有放弃拜占庭式的威严——蓝色的披肩、修长的手指和仪式般的对称都是从东方继承而来——但他让人物转身、低语和倾斜，使衣纹在膝部显得有真实重量，并在宝座后面开辟了一个浅浅的空间。\n\n结果是一幅开始有呼吸感的神圣图像。它表明文艺复兴并非只出现在佛罗伦萨：在锡耶纳，宗教绘画早已成为展示人体动作的舞台。", "maestà (madonna enthroned with saints and angels) 1308 1308–1311 europe 杜乔·迪·博宁塞尼亚 early renaissance / sienese gothic faith human world europe tempera and gold leaf on panel wikimedia commons *maestà* was the front panel of duccio's double-sided altarpiece for siena cathedral, carried through the streets in 1311 like a relic. the virgin sits on a throne with the christ child, surrounded by saints and angels; the gold ground compresses the crowd into a luminous plane. duccio does not abandon byzantine majesty — the blue mantle, long fingers and ceremonial symmetry are inherited from the east — but he lets figures turn, whisper and lean, gives drapery real weight at the knee, and opens a shallow space behind the throne.\n\nthe result is a sacred image that begins to breathe. it shows that the renaissance did not appear only in florence: in siena, devotional painting had already become a stage for human gesture."], "huang-gongwang-summer-mountains-1350": ["《夏山图》 summer mountains (after dong yuan [active c. 937–75]) 1350 1290–1354 中国 元 黄公望 元代文人山水 风景 天地 中国 绢本水墨淡设色 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1290–1354，中国 元。黄公望的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "summer mountains (after dong yuan [active c. 937–75]) 1350 1290–1354 中国 元 黄公望 yuan literati landscape landscape heaven and earth china 绢本水墨淡设色 cleveland museum of art 1290–1354, china. 黄公望; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1992.1. this is a painting (绢本水墨淡设色)."], "huang-gongwang-fuchun-1350": ["《富春山居图》 1350 1347–1350 中国 黄公望 元代文人山水 风景 天地 中国 纸本水墨 维基共享资源 黄公望在七十九岁开始创作《富春山居图》，历时数年完成。淡墨干笔描绘富春江畔的山峦、村落、松林和渔船；笔触松散，像重复呼吸的痕迹。群山不压，人水不喧；整幅画卷仿佛是一段漫长的漫步。\n\n清初，一位收藏家因随葬需将画卷焚毁。幸被救出后，画卷被分为两部分：前段《剩山图》收藏于浙江省博物馆；后段《无用师卷》收藏于台北故宫博物院。它的命运成为中国画史上最著名的“断简之美”。", "dwelling in the fuchun mountains 1350 1347–1350 china 黄公望 yuan literati landscape landscape heaven and earth china ink on paper wikimedia commons dwelling in the fuchun mountains was begun when huang gongwang was seventy-nine and completed over several years. pale ink and dry brush describe mountains, villages, pine groves and fishing boats along the fuchun river; the strokes are loose, like traces of repeated breathing. mountains do not press, water does not clamour; the whole scroll is an extended walk.\n\nin the early qing, a collector had the scroll burned to accompany him in death. rescued, it was split in two: the first section, remaining mountain, is in the zhejiang provincial museum; the later section, the wuyongshi scroll, is in the national palace museum, taipei. its fate became the most famous \"beauty of the fragment\" in chinese painting."], "wang-meng-writing-books-1350": ["《松荫著书图》 writing books under the pine trees 1350 c. 1308–1385 中国 元 王蒙 元代文人山水 风景 天地 中国 纸本水墨设色 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1308–1385，中国 元。王蒙的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "writing books under the pine trees 1350 c. 1308–1385 中国 元 王蒙 yuan literati landscape landscape heaven and earth china 纸本水墨设色 cleveland museum of art c. 1308–1385, china. 王蒙; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1997.94. this is a painting (纸本水墨设色)."], "ni-zan-bamboo-rock-1350": ["《竹石乔柯图》 bamboo, rock, and tall tree 1350 c. 1300s 中国 元 倪瓒 元代文人山水 风景 天地 中国 纸本水墨 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1300s，中国 元。倪瓒的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "bamboo, rock, and tall tree 1350 c. 1300s 中国 元 倪瓒 yuan literati landscape landscape heaven and earth china 纸本水墨 cleveland museum of art c. 1300s, china. 倪瓒; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1978.65. this is a painting (纸本水墨)."], "ni-zan-woods-valleys-1355": ["《渔庄秋霁图》 1355 1355 中国 倪瓒 元代文人山水 风景 天地 中国 纸本水墨 维基共享资源 《玉山林谷》是倪瓒典型的“一江两岸”构图：前景中几棵稀疏的树和一片岩石坡，中央是一片宽阔空旷的水面，远处是低矮的山丘。没有人，也没有船，只有简约的墨迹和一首诗。倪瓒用干笔侧锋，线条轻而粗糙，就像呼吸留在纸上的痕迹。\n\n这种极端的空旷不是不完整，而是他的选择：他把世界缩减到树、石、水和一条天际。晚元的动荡和一个人孤高的纯净都被压进了那个空白中。", "woods and valleys of mount yu 1355 1355 china 倪瓒 yuan literati landscape landscape heaven and earth china ink on paper wikimedia commons woods and valleys of mount yu is ni zan's typical \"one river, two banks\" composition: a few sparse trees and a rocky slope in the foreground, a broad empty expanse of water in the middle, low hills in the distance. there are no people and no boats, only minimal ink and a poem. ni zan uses a dry side-tipped brush; lines are light and rough, like breath left on paper.\n\nthis extreme emptiness is not incompletion but choice: he reduces the world to trees, rock, water and a strip of sky. the turmoil of the late yuan and one man's solitary purity are pressed into that void."], "masaccio-expulsion-1427": ["《逐出伊甸园》 1427 1425–1427 欧洲 马萨乔 早期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 湿壁画 维基共享资源 在佛罗伦萨的布兰恰奇礼拜堂，马萨乔把羞耻表现为身体的重量。亚当和夏娃赤裸，从右侧被驱赶出去；夏娃抬起头，张开嘴，手遮住私处，而亚当低下头，把脸藏在手臂后面，双脚踏在真实的阴影里。几乎没有背景景观，只有一个拱门和一小块地面，但解剖学、透视缩短和强烈的明暗对比让场景异常具体。\n\n它常被称为第一幅真正把人体置于中心的文艺复兴画作：天使的剑向外指去，但真正打动观众的是这两个人物找不到放手和脚的位置。马萨乔在三十岁前去世，但这幅壁画后来成为列奥纳多和米开朗基罗的回归之作。", "the expulsion from the garden of eden 1427 1425–1427 europe 马萨乔 early renaissance faces human world europe fresco wikimedia commons in the brancacci chapel in florence, masaccio made shame a matter of bodily weight. adam and eve, naked, are driven out from the right; eve lifts her head and opens her mouth, her hands covering her sex, while adam bows and hides his face behind his arm, his feet planted in real shadow. there is almost no landscape, only an archway and a strip of ground, yet anatomy, foreshortening and strong chiaroscuro make the scene unusually concrete.\n\nit is often called the first renaissance image to place the human figure truly at its centre: the angel's sword points outward, but what pierces the viewer is the way the two figures can find nowhere to put their hands and feet. masaccio died before he was thirty, yet this fresco became a point of return for leonardo and michelangelo after him."], "van-eyck-arnolfini-1434": ["《阿尔诺芬尼夫妇像》 1434 1434 欧洲 扬·凡·艾克 北方文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（橡木板） 维基共享资源 扬·范·艾克把一个婚姻变成了一个密闭的房间。这对夫妇手牵手站在中央，女人把裙子拉在肚子上；光线从左上方照进来，黄铜吊灯、橘子、床幔、拖鞋以及脚边的小狗都被同等细致地描绘出来。在他们之间的后墙上挂着一面凸面镜，反射着房间和两位见证人；镜子上方的字写着“johannes de eyck fuit hic”——扬·范·艾克在此。\n\n油画颜料被用到了极致：布料、金属和皮肤几乎可以触摸。关于这幅画是记录婚礼、订婚还是纪念，至今仍有争议；但可以确定的是，画家把自己也写进了这个私密空间。", "the arnolfini portrait 1434 1434 europe 扬·凡·艾克 northern renaissance faces human world europe oil on oak panel wikimedia commons jan van eyck turns a marriage into an airtight room. the couple stand hand in hand at the centre, the woman gathering her skirt over her belly; light falls from the upper left, and the brass chandelier, oranges, bed hangings, slippers and the dog at their feet are each rendered with equal attention. on the back wall between them hangs a convex mirror reflecting the room and two witnesses; above it, the inscription reads \"johannes de eyck fuit hic\" — jan van eyck was here.\n\noil paint is pushed to its limit: fabric, metal and skin seem almost tactile. whether the image records a wedding, a betrothal or a memorial is still debated; what is certain is that the painter has written himself into this private space."], "weyden-descent-from-cross-1435": ["《下十字架》 1435 约1435 欧洲 罗希尔·凡·德·魏登 北方文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（木板） 维基共享资源 罗吉耶·范·德·魏登把下十字架的场景压缩在一个浅浅的金色盒子里。基督的身体像弓一样弯曲，几乎与昏倒的圣母平行；亚利马太的约瑟和尼哥底母支撑着他的手臂和腿，约翰在右边哭泣，抹大拉的马利亚拧着手。人物被安排在浮雕般的空间里，每一滴泪水、衣褶和伤口都画得锐利入画。\n\n这一构图将悲伤表现到极致，成为北方文艺复兴宗教绘画的范本。它不追求深远的空间感；它不给观者退路，只留下正视哀悼的责任。", "the descent from the cross 1435 约1435 europe 罗希尔·凡·德·魏登 northern renaissance faces human world europe oil on panel wikimedia commons rogier van der weyden compresses the descent from the cross into a shallow golden box. christ's body curves like a bow, almost parallel to the swooning virgin; joseph of arimathea and nicodemus support his arms and legs, john weeps on the right, and mary magdalene wrings her hands. the figures are arranged in a relief-like enclosure, every tear, fold and wound drawn with a cutting edge.\n\nthis composition, which pushes grief to an extreme, became a model for religious painting in the northern renaissance. it does not seek deep space; it leaves the viewer no exit, only the obligation to face the mourning head-on."], "shen-zhou-loft-mount-lu-1467": ["《庐山高图》 1467 1467 中国 沈周 明代吴门画派 风景 天地 中国 纸本设色 维基共享资源 高耸的庐山是沈周为他的老师陈寬七十岁生日所画的。山几乎高出画面的顶端，用麻织纹理的笔触和由深到淡的墨色描绘；山脚下有一条溪流、几棵松树和一个仰望瀑布的人。右侧题款说明这幅画是为老师的生日所作。\n\n沈周把庐山作为知识和美德的象征，而不仅仅是风景。吴门画派的文人趣味在这里体现为温和却坚定的秩序：山高、水长、人小——但仍在凝视。", "lofty mount lu 1467 1467 china 沈周 ming dynasty wu school landscape heaven and earth china ink and colour on paper wikimedia commons lofty mount lu was painted by shen zhou for his teacher chen kuan's seventieth birthday. the mountain rises almost beyond the top of the picture, built with hemp-fibre texture strokes and ink graded from dark to pale; at its foot are a stream, pines and a figure gazing up at a waterfall. the inscription at the right states that the painting is for a teacher's birthday.\n\nshen zhou makes mount lu a symbol of knowledge and virtue, not merely scenery. the literati taste of the wu school appears here as a gentle but firm order: mountain high, water long, person small — but still looking."], "botticelli-primavera-1480": ["《春》 1480 约1480 欧洲 桑德罗·波提切利 早期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 蛋彩画（木板） 维基共享资源 《春》像一个半开的剧院在慢慢展开。在右边，西风追逐仙女，弗洛拉在画面上撒满鲜花；中央，维纳斯举手祝福，蒙眼的丘比特瞄准她的上方；左边，三美神成圈起舞，而墨丘利背对着我们站在远端。橘树把深色的背景围住，草地上点缀着成百上千种可以辨认的花朵。\n\n波提切利把异教神话、春天的寓意和美第奇宫廷的审美融入到一幅横向叙事画中。画面没有一个中心焦点，但目光、动作和衣饰的节奏把整个构图紧密联系起来。与《维纳斯的诞生》一起，它构成了文艺复兴时期对古代神话最完整、最优雅的诠释。", "primavera 1480 约1480 europe 桑德罗·波提切利 early renaissance faces human world europe tempera on panel wikimedia commons primavera unfolds like a half-open theatre. on the right, zephyr pursues a nymph and flora scatters flowers across the panel; at the centre venus raises a hand in blessing while blindfolded cupid aims above her; on the left the three graces dance in a ring, with mercury, his back to us, at the far edge. orange trees close the dark background, and the grass is studded with hundreds of identifiable flowers.\n\nbotticelli braids pagan myth, spring allegory and medici court taste into a single horizontal narrative. there is no central focus, yet gaze, gesture and the rhythm of drapery hold the composition together. with the birth of venus, it forms the renaissance's most complete and elegant translation of ancient myth."], "botticelli-birth-of-venus-1485": ["《维纳斯的诞生》 1485 约1485 欧洲 桑德罗·波提切利 早期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 蛋彩画（布面） 维基共享资源 维纳斯站在巨大的贝壳上从海中升起，被西风和一位微风女神吹到岸边，而一位时辰女神正等着，手里拿着一件绣着花纹的披肩。波提切利摒弃了中世纪的金色背景，让海水和岸边融入淡蓝和绿色；女神的重量偏向右边，她的头发和衣裳被吹成连续的曲线。解剖学规则被打破：身体被拉长和倾斜，轮廓像雕刻浮雕一样清晰。\n\n这种“非正确的优雅”就是早期文艺复兴时期的理想美，比例来自诗意而非测量。这幅画属于美第奇家族收藏，把异教神话带进了佛罗伦萨的居室，同时也是西方艺术中最常被复制的美的形象之一。", "the birth of venus 1485 约1485 europe 桑德罗·波提切利 early renaissance faces human world europe tempera on canvas wikimedia commons venus rises from the sea on a vast shell, blown ashore by zephyr and a breeze goddess, while one of the horae waits with an embroidered mantle. botticelli abandons the medieval gold ground and lets sea and shore dissolve into pale blue and green; the goddess's weight sits to the right, her hair and drapery blown into continuous curves. anatomy is not obeyed: the body is stretched and tilted, its outline as crisp as a carved relief.\n\nthis \"incorrect elegance\" is the ideal beauty of the early renaissance, proportion derived from poetry rather than measurement. the panel belonged to the medici collection, carried pagan myth into florentine rooms, and remains one of the most reproduced images of beauty in western art."], "leonardo-last-supper-1495": ["《最后的晚餐》 1495 约1495–1498 欧洲 列奥纳多·达·芬奇 盛期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 湿壁画（蛋彩与油） 维基共享资源 在米兰圣玛利亚感恩教堂的食堂墙上，列奥纳多用一点透视法布置了《最后的晚餐》。十二位使徒被分成四组，每组三个人，从中心向外延展。基督刚说过：“你们中有一个将背叛我”；他的双手摊开在桌上，而犹大在阴影中抓着钱包，身体向后倾。消失点位于基督的头部，长桌的线条将每一个声音都引向中心。\n\n因为列奥纳多使用干蛋彩和油画而非真正的湿壁画，这幅画完成不久后就开始剥落。现在所保存的是一幅被时间不断修补的图像；其中的人类心理编排仍然是西方叙事绘画的入门课。", "the last supper 1495 约1495–1498 europe 列奥纳多·达·芬奇 high renaissance faces human world europe tempera and oil on plaster wikimedia commons on the refectory wall of santa maria delle grazie in milan, leonardo stages the last supper in a room built by one-point perspective. the twelve apostles are arranged in four groups of three, rippling outward from the centre. christ has just said, \"one of you will betray me\"; his hands lie open on the table, while judas, in shadow, clutches his purse and leans back. the vanishing point sits at christ's head, and the long table lines gather every voice towards the centre.\n\nbecause leonardo worked in dry tempera and oil rather than true fresco, the painting began to flake soon after completion. what survives is an image endlessly patched by time; its choreography of human psychology remains a primer of western narrative painting."], "bosch-garden-earthly-delights-1500": ["《人间乐园》 1500 约1490–1510 欧洲 希罗尼穆斯·博斯 北方文艺复兴 灾变 世事 欧洲 油画（橡木板三联画） 维基共享资源 《人间乐园》是一幅三联画。左边的画板是伊甸园，上帝把夏娃介绍给亚当；中间是一个挤满成千上万裸体人物的花园，他们在水果、池塘、鸟类和野兽之间玩耍；右边是一个黑暗的地狱，乐器变成折磨人的工具，怪物吞噬人身。合上时，外翼显示的是灰色的创造，世界被包裹在透明球体中。\n\n博斯把中世纪的道德寓言、炼金术符号和民间谚语都塞进了一个视觉机器里，使得快乐与惩罚连成一体。不管这是警告、讽刺，还是对某种被压抑事物的投射，一直没有定论；正是这种难以解读性，使它在五个世纪后仍然吸引观众。", "the garden of earthly delights 1500 约1490–1510 europe 希罗尼穆斯·博斯 northern renaissance disaster world affairs europe oil on oak panels (triptych) wikimedia commons the garden of earthly delights is a triptych. the left panel is eden, where god presents eve to adam; the centre is a garden crowded with thousands of naked figures sporting among fruit, pools, birds and beasts; the right is a dark hell where musical instruments become instruments of torture and monsters devour bodies. closed, the outer wings show a grey creation, the world enclosed in a transparent sphere.\n\nbosch packs medieval moral allegory, alchemical signs and folk proverb into one visual machine, so that pleasure and punishment follow nose to tail. whether it is warning, satire or the projection of something repressed has never been settled; that very resistance to decoding is why it still holds viewers five centuries later."], "durer-self-portrait-1500": ["《自画像（二十八岁）》 1500 1500 欧洲 阿尔布雷希特·丢勒 北方文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（椴木板） 维基共享资源 1500年，丢勒正面、对称地画了自己，目光直视观者：长发和胡须垂落在两侧，像一位基督形象，右手放在胸前。黑色的背景让面部和金发显得格外明亮，毛皮衣领一根根细致描绘。他在右侧署了拉丁铭文和“ad”字母组合，标注了新世纪的起点。\n\n丢勒借用了基督形象的正面构图，并将艺术家的自我意识提升到接近神圣的高度。这被解读为北方文艺复兴肖像的宣言：画家不再只是一个普通工匠，而是获得上帝认可的创造者。", "self-portrait at the age of 28 1500 1500 europe 阿尔布雷希特·丢勒 northern renaissance faces human world europe oil on lime panel wikimedia commons in 1500 dürer painted himself frontally, symmetrically, staring directly at the viewer: long hair and beard falling to either side like a christ figure, his right hand laid across his chest. the black ground makes face and golden hair luminous, and the fur collar is painted hair by hair. the latin inscription and his \"ad\" monogram appear at the right, dated at the threshold of a new century.\n\ndürer borrows the frontal composition of christ imagery and raises the artist's self-awareness to something close to sacred. it is read as a manifesto of the northern renaissance portrait: the painter is no longer a mere craftsman but a creator sanctioned by god."], "leonardo-mona-lisa-1503": ["《蒙娜丽莎》 1503 约1503–1519 欧洲 列奥纳多·达·芬奇 盛期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（杨木板） 维基共享资源 留给观众的不是微笑，而是不确定感：她没有眉毛，眼角和嘴角的轮廓模糊得无法分辨；她身后的地平线两边高度不同，路和水远远延伸。达·芬奇的烟雾法让形态在空气中消散，同时将观众的注意力锁定在脸上。据说她是佛罗伦萨商人的妻子丽莎·杰拉尔迪尼，但她的身份从未得到确切确认。\n\n这幅画在1911年被盗后成为全球知名的画作，现在是卢浮宫参观人数最多的作品。它真正的革命之处在于，一幅肖像不再只是外貌的记录，而是一个似乎会思考、会回望的人。", "mona lisa 1503 约1503–1519 europe 列奥纳多·达·芬奇 high renaissance faces human world europe oil on poplar panel wikimedia commons what stays with the viewer is not the smile but the uncertainty: there are no eyebrows, and the corners of the eyes and mouth are blurred past definition; the horizon behind her sits at different heights on either side, roads and water receding into distance. leonardo's sfumato lets form dissolve into air while pinning the viewer's attention to the face. she is said to be the wife of a florentine merchant, lisa gherardini, though her identity has never been settled.\n\nthe painting became a global image after its theft in 1911 and is now the most visited work in the louvre. its real revolution is that a portrait ceases to be a record of appearance and becomes a person who seems to think and to look back."], "michelangelo-creation-of-adam-1511": ["《创造亚当》 1511 1511–1512 欧洲 米开朗基罗 盛期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 湿壁画 维基共享资源 米开朗基罗将创造的行为压缩到即将触碰的两只手上。亚当半睡半醒地躺在绿色的土地上，他的身体刚刚被点燃；上帝穿过云层飞奔而来，他的斗篷像帆一样鼓起，天使和风围绕着他。在指尖之间留有一条微小的空隙，这条空隙赋予了整个天花板生命力。\n\n通过雕塑般的裸体、剧烈的扭曲和几乎没有背景，米开朗基罗将“按上帝的形象造的人”转化为肉体与精神之间的紧张关系。亚当的目光慵懒而模糊；上帝的目光则急切而专注。在这一瞬间，创作者与被创造者绝不是平等的。", "the creation of adam 1511 1511–1512 europe 米开朗基罗 high renaissance faces human world europe fresco wikimedia commons michelangelo compresses the act of creation into two hands about to touch. adam lies half-awake on green earth, his body only just kindled; god rushes forward through cloud, his mantle swelling like a sail, angels and wind packed around him. a tiny gap remains between the fingertips, and that gap is what charges the whole ceiling.\n\nwith sculptural nudity, violent torsion and almost no setting, michelangelo turns \"man made in god's image\" into a tension between flesh and spirit. adam's gaze is languid and unfocused; god's is urgent and intent. in this instant, creator and created are anything but equal."], "raphael-school-of-athens-1511": ["《雅典学院》 1511 1509–1511 欧洲 拉斐尔 盛期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 湿壁画 维基共享资源 在《署名室》中，拉斐尔描绘了一个理想的古代学术场景。柏拉图和亚里士多德站在中央拱门下，一个指向天堂，另一个指向地球；苏格拉底、毕达哥拉斯、欧几里得和托勒密分别分布在两侧，有的在辩论，有的在计算，有的在倾听。建筑呈现出巴拉曼特式的中央空间，它的透视效果将人群引入深邃的大厅。\n\n拉斐尔把人文主义者对古代知识的想象变成了一场有序的对话，同时允许他的同时代人以不同的形象出现在画面中。平衡并非静止不变：它在手势、目光和身体方向中不断交换。", "the school of athens 1511 1509–1511 europe 拉斐尔 high renaissance faces human world europe fresco wikimedia commons in the stanza della segnatura, raphael painted an ideal academy of antiquity. plato and aristotle stand beneath the central arch, one pointing to heaven, the other to earth; socrates, pythagoras, euclid and ptolemy are distributed to either side, arguing, calculating or listening. the architecture opens as a bramante-like centralised space, its perspective drawing the crowd into a deep hall.\n\nraphael turned the humanists' image of ancient knowledge into an ordered conversation, and allowed his own contemporaries to enter the scene under different guises. the balance is not static: it is continually exchanged through gesture, gaze and the direction of bodies."], "durer-melencolia-i-1514": ["《忧郁 i》 melencolia i 1514 1514 德国 纽伦堡 阿尔布雷希特·丢勒 北方文艺复兴 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 版画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 丢勒把几何、工具、天平与一只缩着的狗放在同一个画面里；忧郁不是情绪，而是一种被工具包围的思考状态。", "melencolia i 1514 1514 德国 纽伦堡 阿尔布雷希特·丢勒 northern renaissance traces craft europe print cleveland museum of art 1514, europe. 阿尔布雷希特·丢勒; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1926.211. this is a print."], "titian-submersion-pharaoh-1549": ["《红海中的法老军队覆灭》 the submersion of pharaoh's army in the red sea 1515 1514–15, printed 1549 意大利 威尼斯 提香（及多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯） 盛期文艺复兴 战火 世事 欧洲 版画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 提香1514—15年设计这幅木刻，1549年由多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯印成；红海分开，法老的军队在右侧被水吞没。", "the submersion of pharaoh's army in the red sea 1515 1514–15, printed 1549 意大利 威尼斯 提香（及多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯） high renaissance war world affairs europe print cleveland museum of art 1514–15, printed 1549, europe. 提香（及多梅尼科·达莱·格雷凯）; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1952.296. this is a print."], "titian-adoration-magi-1520": ["《三王来朝》 adoration of the magi 1520 1500s 意大利 威尼斯 提香（及工作室） 盛期文艺复兴 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1500s，意大利 威尼斯。提香（及工作室）的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "adoration of the magi 1520 1500s 意大利 威尼斯 提香（及工作室） high renaissance faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art 1500s, europe. 提香（及工作室）; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1957.15. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "parmigianino-entombment-1529": ["《下葬》 the entombment 1529 1529–30 意大利 帕尔马 帕米贾尼诺 矫饰主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 版画（蚀刻） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1529–30，意大利 帕尔马。帕米贾尼诺的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "the entombment 1529 1529–30 意大利 帕尔马 帕米贾尼诺 mannerism faces human world europe 版画（蚀刻） cleveland museum of art 1529–30, europe. 帕米贾尼诺; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1985.1. this is a print (版画（蚀刻）)."], "parmigianino-madonna-long-neck-1535": ["《长颈圣母》 1535 约1534–1540 欧洲 帕米贾尼诺 矫饰主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（木板） 维基共享资源 《长颈圣母》把圣母、圣婴和一群天使安排在一个不确定的空间里。圣母坐在中央，脖子拉得异常长，右手触碰着圣婴，但她的身体似乎随时会滑出画框；圣婴体型偏大，睡着的姿势几乎像古代雕塑。右侧一排纤细的柱子没有柱头，背景看起来既像舞台布景又像未完成的建筑。\n\n帕尔米贾尼诺故意打破比例和透视，把优雅推向失衡的边缘。这种美学后来被称为“矫饰主义”，它不再依赖文艺复兴的测量标准，而是依赖线条、姿态以及观者的微妙不适感。", "madonna with the long neck 1535 约1534–1540 europe 帕米贾尼诺 mannerism faces human world europe oil on panel wikimedia commons madonna with the long neck stages the virgin, child and a crowd of angels in an uncertain space. the virgin sits at the centre, her neck stretched impossibly long, her right hand touching the child while her body seems ready to slide out of the frame; the child is oversized, his sleeping pose almost like an antique sculpture. a row of slender columns at the right lacks capitals, and the background reads as both stage set and unfinished architecture.\n\nparmigianino deliberately violates proportion and perspective, pushing grace to the edge of imbalance. this aesthetic, later called mannerism, no longer trusts renaissance measurement; it trusts line, pose and the viewer's unease."], "bronzino-portrait-woman-1550": ["《女子肖像》 portrait of a woman 1550 c. 1550 意大利 佛罗伦萨 阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺 矫饰主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（木板） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1550，意大利 佛罗伦萨。阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "portrait of a woman 1550 c. 1550 意大利 佛罗伦萨 阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺 mannerism faces human world europe 油画（木板） cleveland museum of art c. 1550, europe. 阿尼奥洛·布龙齐诺; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1972.121. this is a painting (油画（木板）)."], "bruegel-tower-of-babel-1563": ["《巴别塔》 1563 1563 欧洲 老彼得·勃鲁盖尔 北方文艺复兴 灾变 世事 欧洲 油画（木板） 维基共享资源 老彼得·勃鲁盖尔将圣经中的巴别塔描绘成一个建筑工地：塔螺旋向上，拱廊、楼梯和脚手架层层叠叠，像蚁穴一样繁忙；顶部还未封闭，红砖和灰石交替出现。在左下方，弥诺陶国王骑着马带着随从到来，而工人们还在搬运石块。老彼得·勃鲁盖尔在这座象征人类傲慢的纪念碑中填满了佛兰德日常细节，让它映射出十六世纪安特卫普的商业狂热和语言分裂的恐惧。塔像切开的一段历史：壮丽，但注定要毁灭。", "the tower of babel 1563 1563 europe 老彼得·勃鲁盖尔 northern renaissance disaster world affairs europe oil on panel wikimedia commons bruegel paints the biblical tower of babel as a building site: the tower spirals upward, its tiers of arcades, stairs and scaffolding swarming like an anthill; the top has not closed, and red brick alternates with grey stone. at the lower left, king nimrod rides in with his retinue while workmen still haul blocks.\n\nbruegel fills this monument to human hubris with flemish everyday detail, and lets it shadow the commercial fever and fear of linguistic division in sixteenth-century antwerp. the tower is cut open like a section through history: magnificent, and doomed."], "bruegel-hunters-in-snow-1565": ["《雪中猎人》 1565 1565 欧洲 老彼得·勃鲁盖尔 北方文艺复兴 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（木板） 维基共享资源 《雪中猎人》是老彼得·勃鲁盖尔一年十二个月系列中最寒冷、最宁静的一幅画。猎人和猎狗从右侧山脊下行，他们的足迹在雪地上拖出一条斜线；左边的村庄屋顶被雪压得下沉，远处的池塘上有人滑冰，灰蓝色的山脉封住了天际线。画面没有中心人物，但视线会沿着山脊、树线和冰面一直延伸到远方。\n\n老彼得·勃鲁盖尔描绘的北方冬日空气仿佛可以呼吸：铅灰色的天空、黑色的树木、脏雪。人类的形象只是风景的一部分，这种“小人物、大自然”的视角在后来的荷兰风景画和浪漫主义中得到了呼应。", "hunters in the snow (winter) 1565 1565 europe 老彼得·勃鲁盖尔 northern renaissance landscape heaven and earth europe oil on panel wikimedia commons hunters in the snow is the coldest and quietest panel of bruegel's series of the months. hunters and dogs descend a ridge from the right, their tracks dragging a diagonal line through the snow; village roofs sag under snow on the left, skaters circle a pond beyond, and grey-blue mountains close the horizon. there is no central figure, yet the eye is led along ridge, treeline and ice into the distance.\n\nbruegel paints northern winter air as something breathable: leaden sky, black trees, dirty snow. the human figures are only part of the landscape, and this \"small people, large nature\" view echoes later through dutch landscape painting and romanticism."], "xu-wei-grapes-1580": ["《墨葡萄图》 1580 约16世纪后期 中国 徐渭 明代写意花鸟 风景 天地 中国 纸本水墨 维基共享资源 《墨葡萄》是徐渭大写意花鸟画的代表作。一串葡萄悬挂在藤蔓上，墨色从深到淡，笔触狂放，甚至每颗葡萄的边界几乎消失；叶子用大笔一挥，像被风撕开的纸。在右边，有一首诗：“半生坎坷，如今老矣；独坐书斋，对着晚风长啸。笔下明珠无处卖——随意抛入野葡萄藤里。”\n\n徐渭的一生波折不断：入狱、发疯、杀妻。他画葡萄是“无人要的珍珠”，也把自己画进了墨里。大写意不只是技法，更是一种把生命赌在纸上的表达。", "ink grapes 1580 约16世纪后期 china 徐渭 ming dynasty expressive flower painting landscape heaven and earth china ink on paper wikimedia commons ink grapes is the representative work of xu wei's grand xieyi flower painting. a cluster of grapes hangs from a vine, ink running from dark to pale, the brush wild until individual grapes almost lose their edges; leaves are swept with a broad brush like paper torn by wind. at the right, a poem: \"half a life in failure, now an old man; alone in my study i howl at the evening wind. the bright pearls under my brush have nowhere to be sold — tossed idly into the wild vines.\"\n\nxu wei's life was turbulent: imprisonment, madness, the killing of his wife. he painted grapes as \"pearls no one wants\" and painted himself into that ink. grand xieyi becomes more than technique: an expression that stakes a life on paper."], "caravaggio-judith-1599": ["《朱迪斯斩首荷罗孚尼》 1599 约1598–1599 欧洲 卡拉瓦乔 巴洛克 战火 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 卡拉瓦乔将圣经中的刺杀变成了床边的谋杀。朱迪思站在右侧，一手抓着荷罗孚尼斯的头发，另一只手握着剑;她的脸皱起，眉头紧锁，厌恶与恐惧交织在一起。将军的身体在床上扭转，嘴巴张开，鲜血从脖子喷射到白色床单上。女仆阿布拉在左侧等着，手提包，神情紧张。\n\n卡拉瓦乔拒绝美化这一英雄行为：朱迪思不是寓言，而是一个施展力量、感到恐惧的女性。极端明暗对比将背景压入黑色，仅留下皮肤、亚麻布和血迹在光线中。", "judith beheading holofernes 1599 约1598–1599 europe 卡拉瓦乔 baroque war world affairs europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons caravaggio turns the biblical assassination into a murder at the bedside. judith stands on the right, one hand gripping holofernes' hair, the other holding the sword; her face recoils, brows knitted, disgust and fear together. the general's body twists on the bed, mouth open, blood jetting from the neck onto white sheets. the maid abra waits at the left, bag in hand, tense.\n\ncaravaggio refuses to beautify the heroic act: judith is not an allegory but a woman exerting force and feeling afraid. extreme chiaroscuro presses the background into black, leaving only skin, linen and blood in the light."], "caravaggio-calling-of-matthew-1600": ["《圣马太蒙召》 1600 1599–1600 欧洲 卡拉瓦乔 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《圣马太的召唤》发生在一个昏暗的罗马税吏室中。基督从右侧进入，举起手；一道光束随着他的手势，穿过桌子照在马太身上。马太坐在桌子后面，指着自己，好像在问：“是我吗？”他身旁的一个年轻人正在数钱，另外两个人继续交谈。桌子、凳子、钱袋和羽毛笔都被画得很普通。\n\n卡拉瓦乔把这个神圣的时刻置于最世俗的房间里，让光线而不是构图完成召唤。光束照亮了马太，在桌子上划出一条不可回头的线。", "the calling of saint matthew 1600 1599–1600 europe 卡拉瓦乔 baroque faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the calling of saint matthew takes place in a dim roman tax collector's room. christ enters from the right and raises a hand; a shaft of light follows the gesture, crossing the table and landing on matthew. seated behind the table, matthew points at himself as if asking, \"who, me?\" a young man beside him counts coins, two others continue talking. table, stool, money bag and quill are painted as ordinary objects.\n\ncaravaggio places the sacred moment in the most worldly of rooms and lets light, rather than composition, perform the calling. the beam illuminates matthew and draws a line at the table from which there is no turning back."], "el-greco-view-of-toledo-1600": ["《托莱多风景》 1600 约1599–1600 欧洲 埃尔·格列柯 矫饰主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 埃尔·格列柯的《托莱多的景色》没有描绘城市最显眼的地标——大教堂，而是画出一座被风暴围困的城市。阿尔卡萨尔坐落在左侧的小山上，房顶和尖塔挤满了画面的中间，而塔霍河绕到右侧。天空占据了大部分画布，呈铅灰色和绿色翻滚，一道闪电划破天际。\n\n这更像是一幅内心的风景画，而不是地理肖像。埃尔·格列柯舍弃了意大利式的纵深感，让城市漂浮在黑夜中；建筑被拉长和扭曲，边缘模糊不清。托莱多不再是单纯的地理地点，而是信仰与衰败的象征。", "view of toledo 1600 约1599–1600 europe 埃尔·格列柯 mannerism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons el greco's view of toledo omits the city's most obvious landmark, the cathedral, and paints instead a city besieged by storm. the alcázar sits on a hill at the left, roofs and spires crowd the middle, and the tagus bends around the right. sky occupies most of the canvas, rolling in lead and green, a lightning bolt cracking through it.\n\nthis is less a topographic portrait than an inner landscape. el greco abandons italianate depth and lets the city float in night; buildings are stretched and twisted, their edges uncertain. toledo becomes not geography but a symbol of faith and decline together."], "el-greco-christ-cross-1600": ["《十字架上的基督》 christ on the cross 1605 c. 1600–1610 西班牙 托莱多 埃尔·格列柯 矫饰主义 灾变 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1600–1610，西班牙 托莱多。埃尔·格列柯的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "christ on the cross 1605 c. 1600–1610 西班牙 托莱多 埃尔·格列柯 mannerism disaster world affairs europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art c. 1600–1610, europe. 埃尔·格列柯; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1952.222. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "rubens-descent-from-cross-1614": ["《下十字架》 1614 1612–1614 欧洲 彼得·保罗·鲁本斯 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（木板） 维基共享资源 鲁本斯的《基督下十字架》，是为安特卫普大教堂创作的三联画的中央面板，展示了基督的身体沿着十字架斜滑下，被白色布料承托。亚利马太的约瑟夫和尼哥底母从上方拉拽布料，约翰在下方接住双足，圣母、抹大拉的马利亚和其他妇女跪在左侧。人物形成一个旋转的菱形，光线沿着布料和肌肉流动。\n\n鲁本斯将巴洛克的重量感、运动感和血腥感推向极致：这不是安静的哀悼，而是仍在进行中的拉拽。白色布料既是裹尸布也是反光板，让所有视线都集中在身体上。", "the descent from the cross 1614 1612–1614 europe 彼得·保罗·鲁本斯 baroque faces human world europe oil on panel wikimedia commons rubens's descent from the cross, the central panel of a triptych for antwerp cathedral, shows christ's body sliding diagonally from the cross, caught in a white sheet. joseph of arimathea and nicodemus haul the cloth from above, john receives the feet below, and the virgin, mary magdalene and other women kneel at the left. the figures form a rotating diamond, light running along the sheet and across muscle.\n\nrubens pushes baroque weight, motion and blood to an extreme: this is not quiet mourning but a hauling that is still under way. the white cloth is both shroud and reflector, turning every gaze towards the body."], "artemisia-judith-1620": ["《朱迪斯斩首荷罗孚尼》 1620 约1620 欧洲 阿尔泰米西娅·真蒂莱斯基 巴洛克 战火 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 阿尔特米西亚·詹蒂莱斯基的《朱迪斯斩首荷罗孚尼》比卡拉瓦乔的处理更具身体感和亲密感。朱迪斯站在床边，卷起袖子到肘部，双手用力按住将军的肩膀和头发；女仆阿布拉从上方压住他的身体，两位女性在完成一项必须完成的任务。鲜血顺着床单流下，染红了朱迪斯的袖口。\n\n画家本人在1611年的一次审判中被迫描述了一起强奸事件，这幅画常被解读为复仇之作。不管这种解读是不是有些过头，两个女性共同施力的构图在17世纪的绘画中是极其罕见的。", "judith slaying holofernes 1620 约1620 europe 阿尔泰米西娅·真蒂莱斯基 baroque war world affairs europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons artemisia gentileschi's judith beheading holofernes is more physical and more intimate than caravaggio's treatment. judith stands at the bed, sleeves pushed to the elbow, both arms bearing down on the general's shoulder and hair; the maid abra presses his body from above, the two women completing a task that must be completed. blood runs down the sheet and stains judith's cuff.\n\nthe painter herself was forced to describe a rape during a 1611 trial, and the picture is often read as revenge. whether or not that reading is pressed too far, the composition of two women exerting force together is extremely rare in seventeenth-century painting."], "velazquez-jester-calabazas-1632": ["《弄臣卡拉巴萨斯肖像》 portrait of the jester calabazas 1632 c. 1631–32 西班牙 马德里 迭戈·委拉斯开兹 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 卡拉巴萨斯是西班牙宫廷里的弄臣；委拉斯开兹没有把他画成笑话，而是让他坐在光里，手里攥着一只小葫芦。", "portrait of the jester calabazas 1632 c. 1631–32 西班牙 马德里 迭戈·委拉斯开兹 baroque faces human world europe oil painting cleveland museum of art c. 1631–32, europe. 迭戈·委拉斯开兹; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1965.15. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "rembrandt-night-watch-1642": ["《夜巡》 1642 1642 欧洲 伦勃朗 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《夜巡》实际上并不是夜晚的场景。一支民兵队伍正从阿姆斯特丹的拱门里出发。队长弗朗斯·班宁克·考克穿着黑色外套，系着红色腰带，正伸手去碰他的中尉威廉·范·鲁伊滕堡的手套，中尉穿着黄色，手指着画框之外的长矛。一些人在打鼓，有些人在升旗，有些人在操纵武器；人群中间被光照到的小女孩格外显眼。\n\n伦勃朗拒绝了传统的按排排列的群像画，而是把整个队伍描绘成一个集结的瞬间。光影在队伍中流动；每个人都在动作中，每个人都被看见。后来被称为“夜巡”，那是因为上过暗色清漆；清洗后才显现出白天出发的场景。", "the night watch 1642 1642 europe 伦勃朗 baroque faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the night watch is not actually a night scene. a militia company marches out of an amsterdam archway. captain frans banninck cocq, in black with a red sash, reaches towards the glove of his lieutenant, willem van ruytenburch, who wears yellow and points a lance beyond the frame. some men drum, some raise a flag, some handle weapons; a small girl is picked out by light in the middle of the crowd.\n\nrembrandt refuses the conventional row-by-row group portrait and paints the company as a moment of assembly. light and shadow move through the crowd; everyone is in motion and everyone is seen. the later title \"night watch\" came from darkened varnish; cleaning revealed a daytime departure."], "poussin-holy-family-steps-1648": ["《台阶上的圣家族》 the holy family on the steps 1648 1648 法国 巴黎 尼古拉·普桑 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1648，法国 巴黎。尼古拉·普桑的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "the holy family on the steps 1648 1648 paris, france 尼古拉·普桑 baroque faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art 1648, europe. 尼古拉·普桑; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1981.18. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "velazquez-las-meninas-1656": ["《宫娥》 1656 1656 欧洲 迭戈·委拉斯开兹 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《宫娥》将观众置于国王的视线之中。在画面的中央，小公主玛格丽塔由两位宫女照料；右边站着一个侏儒和一只半睡的狗。左边，委拉斯开兹本人站在一幅巨大的画布后面，手持画笔，胸前佩戴圣地亚哥勋章。背墙的镜子中映出了国王和王后，他们正站在观众所在的位置。\n\n通过镜子、门口和多层视线，委拉斯开兹把“谁在看谁”作为画作的主题。这既是一幅宫廷群像，也是关于绘画的画作：画家在画什么，观众站在哪里，都被留在了画框之外。", "las meninas 1656 1656 europe 迭戈·委拉斯开兹 baroque faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons las meninas puts the viewer inside the king's gaze. at the centre, the young infanta margarita is attended by two maids of honour; to the right stand a dwarf and a half-awake dog. on the left, velázquez himself works behind a huge canvas, brush in hand, the order of santiago on his chest. in the mirror on the back wall appear the king and queen, standing exactly where the viewer stands.\n\nwith a mirror, a doorway and several layers of gaze, velázquez makes \"who is looking at whom\" the subject of the picture. it is at once a court group portrait and a painting about painting: what the painter is painting, and where the viewer stands, are both left outside the frame."], "vermeer-view-of-delft-1660": ["《代尔夫特风景》 1660 约1659–1661 欧洲 约翰内斯·维米尔 巴洛克 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《代尔夫特的风景》展示了雨后的城市景象。天空占据了画布的大部分，云朵从灰蓝色变化到奶油色，阳光轻轻照在远处的屋顶和尖塔上。前景的运河和码头仍笼罩在阴影中，停靠着船只，几个人站在水边。新城的红砖和老城的灰瓦被一条水线分隔开来。\n\n维米尔用几乎看不见的笔触将光分解：屋顶不是单一的颜色，而是由数百道微小的笔触组成。后来的画家称它为世界上最美的画之一，不是因为宏伟，而是因为它让普通的城市在光影中看起来值得铭记。", "view of delft 1660 约1659–1661 europe 约翰内斯·维米尔 baroque landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons view of delft shows the city after rain. sky fills most of the canvas, clouds shifting from grey-blue to cream, light touching distant roofs and spires. the canal and quay in the foreground remain in shadow, with boats moored and a few figures standing at the water's edge. red brick of the new town and grey tile of the old are separated by a line of water.\n\nvermeer atomises light with an almost invisible touch: a roof is not a single colour but hundreds of tiny strokes. later painters called it one of the most beautiful paintings in the world, not for grandeur but for making an ordinary city seem worth remembering in the light."], "vermeer-girl-pearl-earring-1665": ["《戴珍珠耳环的少女》 1665 约1665 欧洲 约翰内斯·维米尔 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《戴珍珠耳环的少女》是一幅类型画（类型画），而不是某位特定人物的肖像，更像是对类型和表情的练习。少女回头看向我们，嘴微张；蓝色头巾和黄色衣服形成冷暖对比，珍珠在她的脖子上捕捉到一点高光，就好像它是房间里唯一的光源。背景是一片深色，没有窗户，也没有家具。\n\n维米尔没有赋予她身份；他只呈现了被看到的瞬间，好像她正要开口说话或正要转身离开。正是这种悬而未决，使这幅画在三个多世纪里一直紧绷着观者的视线。", "girl with a pearl earring 1665 约1665 europe 约翰内斯·维米尔 baroque faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons girl with a pearl earring is a tronie, not a portrait of a named sitter but an exercise in type and expression. the girl turns her head back towards us, lips parted; the blue turban and yellow garment set up a cold-warm contrast, and the pearl catches a small highlight at her neck, as if it were the only light source in the room. the background is a dark field with no window, no furniture.\n\nvermeer does not give her an identity; he gives only the instant of being seen, as if she is about to speak or about to turn away. that suspension has kept the picture taut for more than three centuries."], "rembrandt-self-portrait-1669": ["《双圆自画像》 1669 约1665–1669 欧洲 伦勃朗 巴洛克 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《双圆自画像》是伦勃朗晚期自画像中最安静的一幅。他坐在画架前，手握画笔和调色板，转向观众；在他身后的墙上，两圈淡色的圆圈像几何练习或未完成的宣言一样被描绘着。脸部有光照，眼角和嘴角向下，皮肤已经不再年轻。\n\n伦勃朗画了数十幅自画像；这幅没有戏剧性的动作，只有一个人在自己的工作室里平静地面对衰老。那两个圆圈的意义从未得到确定；它们像未解的方程一样留在画面上。", "self-portrait with two circles 1669 约1665–1669 europe 伦勃朗 baroque faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons self-portrait with two circles is the quietest of rembrandt's late self-portraits. he sits at his easel with brush and palette, turning towards the viewer; on the wall behind, two circles are sketched in pale paint, like a geometry exercise or an unfinished manifesto. the face is lit, the corners of eye and mouth drawn down, the skin no longer young.\n\nrembrandt painted dozens of self-portraits; this one has no dramatic action, only a man in his studio facing old age calmly. what the two circles mean has never been settled; they leave the picture like an equation still to be solved."], "shitao-thirty-six-peaks-1705": ["《黄山三十六峰图》 1705 约1705 中国 石涛 清初个性派 风景 天地 中国 纸本水墨 维基共享资源 《黄山三十六峰图》是石涛的一幅晚年挂轴作品，凭记忆创作完成。画面层次向上堆叠：前景有松树和茅屋，中景有巨石、溪流和云雾，高峰几乎延伸至画面顶端。干湿笔交替使用，墨色由浓黑到浅灰，如同被雾气冲洗；右上方有一段长款，记载了作画的缘由。\n\n石涛曾多次游历黄山，晚年在扬州凭记忆重绘。他并不描绘某一特定的山峰，而是将山的奇特压缩在一笔之中：山峰转折，云雾破散，树木倾斜。在他的《画语录》中，他提出了“一笔”的理念——世界由一笔开始并由这一笔维系；这幅画就是那“一笔”的可视化。", "thirty-six peaks of mount huang recollected 1705 约1705 china 石涛 early qing individualist painting landscape heaven and earth china ink on paper wikimedia commons thirty-six peaks of mount huang recollected is a late hanging scroll by shitao, painted from memory. the composition stacks upward: pines and a thatched hut in the foreground, boulders, stream and cloud in the middle, peak heads receding almost to the top edge. wet and dry brush alternate, ink running from dense black to pale grey as if washed by mist; a long inscription at the upper right records the occasion.\n\nshitao travelled through huangshan many times and repainted it from memory in yangzhou in old age. he does not reproduce a particular peak but compresses the mountain's strangeness into a stroke: mountains turn, clouds break, trees lean. in his huayulu he proposed \"one-stroke\" — the world begins and is held together by a single brushstroke; this painting is that \"one\" made visible."], "watteau-romancer-study-1716": ["《〈说书人〉习作》 study for \"the romancer\" (le conteur) 1716 c. 1716 法国 巴黎 让-安托万·华托 洛可可 面孔 人间 欧洲 素描 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 这是华托为《说书人》准备的红粉笔习作；人物的姿态先被单独研究，再被放进一幅风俗画的关系里。", "study for \"the romancer\" (le conteur) 1716 c. 1716 paris, france 让-安托万·华托 rococo faces human world europe drawing cleveland museum of art c. 1716, europe. 让-安托万·华托; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1928.661. this is a drawing."], "watteau-pilgrimage-cythera-1717": ["《舟发西苔岛》 1717 1717 欧洲 让-安托万·华托 洛可可 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《锡特拉的朝圣》描绘了一群恋人准备离开爱情之岛的场景。他们穿着丝绸和丝带，缓慢地穿过花丛和树林，走向岸边的一艘小船；维纳斯的雕像上挂满了花环，而船夫手持长篙做好了准备。人物从右到左呈起伏的线条，有的回头，有的依旧相拥。\n\n瓦托将爱情描绘成一种即将结束的氛围，而不是一个故事。这种题材，被称为“户外雅集”，融合了洛可可的轻盈感和一种难以言喻的忧郁：快乐已经在渐渐远去。", "pilgrimage to cythera 1717 1717 europe 让-安托万·华托 rococo faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons pilgrimage to cythera shows a group of lovers preparing to leave the island of love. dressed in silk and ribbon, they move slowly through flowers and trees towards a boat at the shore; the statue of venus is garlanded, and a boatman stands ready with his pole. the figures form a rising and falling line from right to left, some turning back, some still embracing.\n\nwatteau paints love as an atmosphere about to end rather than a story. this genre, the fête galante, carries rococo lightness together with an indefinable melancholy: the pleasure is already receding."], "castiglione-hundred-horses-1728": ["《百骏图》 1728 1728 中国 郎世宁 清代宫廷绘画 风景 天地 中国 绢本设色 维基共享资源 《百马图》是意大利耶稣会士朱塞佩·卡斯蒂廖内在清朝宫廷绘制的手卷。百余匹马分布在草坡、溪流和树林间：有的站立，有的打滚，有的饮水，有的由牧人牵引。它们的身体通过细腻的明暗塑造，而树木、岩石和地面则保留了中国画的质感笔触和留白。\n\n卡斯蒂廖内将欧洲的透视、解剖学和明暗对比引入宫廷画，同时必须与中国的材料和观画习惯妥协。结果是混合的视觉效果：马是立体的，空间却是平面的；写实与装饰在同一卷轴中并存。", "one hundred horses 1728 1728 china 郎世宁 qing court painting landscape heaven and earth china ink and colour on silk wikimedia commons one hundred horses is a handscroll painted at the qing court by the italian jesuit giuseppe castiglione. more than a hundred horses are dispersed across grassy slopes, streams and trees: standing, rolling, drinking, led by herdsmen. their bodies are modelled with fine light and shade, while trees, rocks and ground retain chinese texture strokes and reserved space.\n\ncastiglione brought european perspective, anatomy and chiaroscuro into court painting, and was obliged to compromise with chinese materials and viewing habits. the result is a hybrid vision: horses in the round, space flat; realism and ornament in the same scroll."], "chardin-the-ray-1728": ["《鳐鱼》 1728 1728 欧洲 让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹 洛可可 日常 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 夏尔丹的《鳐鱼》是他于1728年为皇家艺术学院提交的展览作品，也是他对静物画的一种宣言。一条被剖开的鳐鱼挂在钩子上，银色的腹部翻开，红色的内脏溢出；左边有只猫在牡蛎壳间行走，而右边放着瓶子、罐子、刀和一块白布。所有物品都摆放在粗糙的石板上。没有神话，也没有寓意，只有厨房的气味。\n\n夏尔丹用厚重的白色高光表现鱼的湿润皮肤，并用深棕色背景将物体衬托得更突出。他让日常事物值得被注视，为库尔贝和马奈对普通事物的尊重铺平了道路。", "the ray (la raie) 1728 1728 europe 让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹 rococo daily life human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons chardin's *the ray* was his reception piece for the royal academy in 1728, and a manifesto for still life. a gutted ray hangs from a hook, its silver belly opened, red entrails spilling; a cat steps among oyster shells on the left, while bottles, a jar, a knife and a white cloth occupy the right. everything sits on a rough stone ledge. there is no myth and no allegory, only the smell of a kitchen.\n\nchardin uses thick white highlights for the wet skin of the fish and a dark brown ground to push the objects forward. he makes the everyday worth looking at, preparing the way for courbet and manet's respect for ordinary things."], "chardin-kitchen-utensils-1734": ["《厨房用具、韭葱、鱼与鸡蛋》 kitchen utensils with leeks, fish, and eggs 1734 c. 1734 法国 巴黎 让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹 洛可可 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1734，法国 巴黎。让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "kitchen utensils with leeks, fish, and eggs 1734 c. 1734 paris, france 让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹 rococo traces craft europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art c. 1734, europe. 让-巴蒂斯特-西梅翁·夏尔丹; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1980.37. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "boucher-music-dance-1740": ["《音乐、舞蹈与丘比特的密谋》 music and dance and cupids in conspiracy 1745 1740s 法国 巴黎 弗朗索瓦·布歇 洛可可 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1740s，法国 巴黎。弗朗索瓦·布歇的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "music and dance and cupids in conspiracy 1745 1740s paris, france 弗朗索瓦·布歇 rococo faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art 1740s, europe. 弗朗索瓦·布歇; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1948.181. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "fragonard-the-swing-1767": ["《秋千》 1767 约1767–1768 欧洲 让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔 洛可可 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《荡秋千》将洛可可风格的轻佻发挥到极致。一位年轻女子坐在树荫下的秋千上，裙摆飞扬，一只鞋踢向空中；她的情人从左边的灌木丛中探出身子向上看，而一位年长的男子在右后方拉着绳子，显然浑然不觉。周围是茂密的叶子，光线像舞台灯光一样照在她的粉色裙子上。\n\n弗拉戈纳尔用旋转的构图、飞扬的衣布和偷看者的视角，让画面内容充满戏剧性。这幅画既是18世纪贵族娱乐的记录，也成为最著名、最容易模仿的洛可可艺术形象。", "the swing 1767 约1767–1768 europe 让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔 rococo faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the swing takes rococo frivolity to its limit. a young woman sits on a swing in the shade, her skirt flying, one shoe kicked into the air; her lover leans out of the bushes at the left to look up, while an older man pulls the ropes at the right rear, apparently unaware. foliage encloses the scene, and light falls like stage lighting on the pink dress.\n\nfragonard uses a swirling composition, lifted cloth and a voyeur's gaze to make play the entire content of the picture. it is both a record of eighteenth-century aristocratic amusement and the most famous, most imitable image of rococo art."], "david-young-woman-turban-1780": ["《戴头巾的年轻女子》 young woman with a turban 1780 c. 1780 法国 巴黎 雅克-路易·大卫 新古典主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1780，法国 巴黎。雅克-路易·大卫的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "young woman with a turban 1780 c. 1780 paris, france 雅克-路易·大卫 neoclassicism faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art c. 1780, europe. 雅克-路易·大卫; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1952.542. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "fragonard-boy-red-cloak-1780": ["《披红衬斗篷的男孩》 a boy in a red-lined cloak 1782 1780s 法国 巴黎 让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔 洛可可 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（木板） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1780s，法国 巴黎。让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "a boy in a red-lined cloak 1782 1780s paris, france 让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔 rococo faces human world europe 油画（木板） cleveland museum of art 1780s, europe. 让-奥诺雷·弗拉戈纳尔; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1942.49. this is a painting (油画（木板）)."], "david-oath-of-horatii-1784": ["《荷拉斯兄弟之誓》 1784 1784 欧洲 雅克-路易·大卫 新古典主义 权利 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《霍拉提兄弟的誓言》把罗马历史中的一个瞬间变成了舞台剧。三个兄弟肩并肩站在父亲面前，手臂伸向剑；父亲举起三把剑，背后是拱门和阴影。右侧，女人们一起倒下，母亲和姐妹低下头，知道战争会让她们失去兄弟或丈夫。\n\n大卫用垂直的柱子、硬朗的轮廓和几乎无笔触的画面，把新古典主义的“美德”变成了几何形状。男性的身体是直线，女性的身体是曲线；誓言和悲伤在画布的两侧被区分开来。", "oath of the horatii 1784 1784 europe 雅克-路易·大卫 neoclassicism rights world affairs europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons oath of the horatii turns a moment of roman history into theatre. three brothers stand shoulder to shoulder before their father, arms extended towards the swords; the father raises the three blades, an archway and shadow behind him. on the right, the women collapse together, mother and sisters bowing their heads, knowing the war will cost them brothers or husbands.\n\ndavid uses vertical columns, hard contours and a nearly brushless surface to turn neoclassical \"virtue\" into geometry. male bodies are straight lines, female bodies curves; oath and grief are divided between the two sides of the canvas."], "utamaro-three-beauties-1793": ["《三位美人》 1793 约1793 东亚 喜多川歌麿 浮世绘 面孔 人间 东亚 木版画 维基共享资源 《三位美人》是喜多川歌磨的大头画（大头画）的代表作。画中三位著名女性并排而立：玉屋的富士本丰姬、浪屋喜多，以及高岛大久。如她们的面容、发型、和服花纹与目光各不相同；背景使用云母粉，使深色背景闪闪发光，衬托出她们的面庞。\n\n歌磨画的不是地位，而是名气：这些女性被城市所关注、讨论和注视。大头画的形式将肖像放大至半身，使观者不得不与她们对视，也让浮世绘从叙事转向一种现代的明星形象。", "three beauties of the present day 1793 约1793 east asia 喜多川歌麿 ukiyo-e faces human world east asia woodblock print wikimedia commons three beauties of the present day is the representative work of kitagawa utamaro's ōkubi-e (large-head pictures). three celebrated women are placed side by side: tomimoto toyohina of the tamaya, naniwaya kita, and takashima ohisa. their faces, hairstyles, robe patterns and glances differ; mica powder in the background makes a shimmering dark ground from which the faces emerge.\n\nutamaro paints not status but fame itself: women who are consumed, discussed and looked at by the city. the large-head format enlarges the portrait to half-length, forcing the viewer to meet their eyes, and turns ukiyo-e from narrative toward a modern kind of star image."], "david-death-of-marat-1793": ["《马拉之死》 1793 1793 欧洲 雅克-路易·大卫 新古典主义 战火 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《马拉之死》把一位被暗杀的政治家变成了烈士。马拉躺在浴缸里死去，身体沿着对角线滑落，右手仍握着羽毛笔，左手拿着写有请愿人名字的请愿书；木块上放着墨水瓶、文件和一把刀。背景是一片空荡的黑暗，没有街道，也没有刺客。\n\n大卫省略了现场的血腥和混乱，只留下一个安静的躯体，看起来几乎像宗教圣像。这是革命宣传的典范：它不报道事实，而是制造一个值得相信的形象。", "the death of marat 1793 1793 europe 雅克-路易·大卫 neoclassicism war world affairs europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the death of marat turns an assassinated politician into a martyr. marat lies dead in his bath, body sliding along the diagonal, quill still in his right hand, a petition with a supplicant's name in his left; on the wooden block sit inkwell, papers and a knife. the background is a blank dark field, with no street and no assassin.\n\ndavid omits the blood and chaos of the scene, leaving only a quiet body that reads almost like an icon. it is the model of revolutionary propaganda: it does not report facts, it manufactures an image worth believing in."], "goya-third-of-may-1814": ["《1808年5月3日》 1814 1814 欧洲 弗朗西斯科·戈雅 浪漫主义 战火 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《五月三日》记录了拿破仑军队在马德里对平民的夜间处决。画面左侧，一排士兵举起火枪，背对观众；画面右侧，一些被处决者已经倒下，另一些用手遮住脸，而中央一个穿白衬衫的男子张开双臂，直视枪口。他身后的灯笼把黑暗变成了舞台。\n\n戈雅画的不是什么英雄的胜利，而是恐惧、鲜血和无法抵抗的躯体。白衣男子的光线像基督一般照在身上，但他并非神性，只是一个即将死亡的人。这幅画常被认为是现代战争形象的开端：不再是将军，而是被杀的人。", "the third of may 1808 1814 1814 europe 弗朗西斯科·戈雅 romanticism war world affairs europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the third of may 1808 records a night execution of civilians by napoleon's troops in madrid. on the left, a rank of soldiers raises muskets, backs to the viewer; on the right, some of the condemned have already fallen, others cover their faces, and at the centre a man in a white shirt throws his arms wide and looks straight into the guns. a lantern behind him turns the darkness into a stage.\n\ngoya paints not the triumph of heroes but fear, blood and bodies that cannot resist. the man in white is lit like a christ, yet he is not divine, only a person about to die. the picture is often taken as the beginning of the modern image of war: no longer generals, but the killed."], "ingres-grande-odalisque-1814": ["《大宫女》 1814 1814 欧洲 让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔 新古典主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《大宫女》展示了一位女子半躺在长沙发上。她背对着我们，头回过肩看，蓝色头巾和金色布料包裹着身体；孔雀羽扇、水烟和帷幕填满了封闭的室内空间。她的脊柱被拉长，右腿多了一个关节，身体的曲线挑战了人体解剖学。\n\ningres并不在意解剖的准确性；他追求的是连续的线条和光滑的肌肤。这幅画将“东方”想象成一个懒散、可观赏的空间，并将新古典主义的线条推进到抽象的边界。", "la grande odalisque 1814 1814 europe 让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔 neoclassicism faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons la grande odalisque shows a concubine reclining on a divan. her back is turned, her head over her shoulder, blue turban and gold fabric enclosing the body; a peacock fan, hookah and drapery fill a closed interior. her spine is elongated, the right leg gains an extra joint, and the curve of the body defies anatomy.\n\ningres does not care about anatomical correctness; he wants continuous line and smooth skin. the painting imagines \"the orient\" as a languid, viewable space, and pushes neoclassical line to the edge of abstraction."], "auto-d49e9fd0": ["《橙与书》静物 still life with orange and book still life with orange and book 1815 1815 跨地域 raphaelle peale 美国静物画 痕迹 技艺 跨地域 绘画 维基共享资源 《橙与书》静物》是拉斐尔·皮尔约1815年的美国静物画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“橙与书》静物”为题，属于美国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "still life with orange and book 1815 1815 cross-regional raphaelle peale american still life traces craft cross-regional painting wikimedia commons 1815, cross-regional. 拉斐尔·皮尔; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:still life with orange and book-raphaelle peale.jpg. this is a painting."], "david-cupid-psyche-1817": ["《丘比特与普绪克》 cupid and psyche 1817 1817 法国 巴黎 雅克-路易·大卫 新古典主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1817，法国 巴黎。雅克-路易·大卫的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "cupid and psyche 1817 1817 paris, france 雅克-路易·大卫 neoclassicism faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art 1817, europe. 雅克-路易·大卫; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1962.37. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "friedrich-wanderer-1818": ["《雾海上的漫游者》 1818 约1818 欧洲 卡斯帕·大卫·弗里德里希 浪漫主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《迷雾海上的漫步者》把一个男人放在岩石高峰上，他背对我们，面对翻腾的迷雾海。他穿着深绿色外套，拄着拐杖，头发被风吹起；远处的山峰像岛屿或未知的边界一样从雾中升起。下方是深谷，上方是苍白的天空。弗里德里希用“背影人物”让观者与画中的人物一起凝视。这个男人既不是英雄也不是游客，而是在无限面前失去尺度感的人。浪漫主义的崇高正是这种混合了宏大与不安的感觉。", "wanderer above the sea of fog 1818 约1818 europe 卡斯帕·大卫·弗里德里希 romanticism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons wanderer above the sea of fog places a man on a rocky summit, his back to us, facing a churning sea of mist. he wears a dark green coat, leans on a cane, hair blown by wind; distant peaks rise through the fog like islands or unknown borders. below is a deep valley, above a pale sky.\n\nfriedrich uses the rückenfigur to make the viewer gaze with the figure in the painting. this man is neither hero nor tourist but someone who loses his sense of scale before the infinite. the romantic sublime is exactly this grandeur mixed with unease."], "goya-saturn-1820": ["《农神吞噬其子》 1820 1819–1823 欧洲 弗朗西斯科·戈雅 浪漫主义 灾变 世事 欧洲 油画（壁画转布面） 维基共享资源 《萨图恩吞食自己的儿子》是戈雅黑色画作中最令人震惊的一幅。萨图恩看起来像个疯狂的老头，眼睛瞪大，嘴巴张开，双手紧握着一个已经被啃掉头和胳膊的小尸体。背景是黑色的，只有肉体和白布捕捉到光线。\n\n晚年的戈雅把自己关在索尔多庄园里，把这些作品直接画在墙上。它们既不是接受委托也不是为展览而作，更像是一个人在与恐惧斗争的私人记录。神话在这里失去了寓意，只剩下暴力本身。", "saturn devouring his son 1820 1819–1823 europe 弗朗西斯科·戈雅 romanticism disaster world affairs europe oil on plaster transferred to canvas wikimedia commons saturn devouring his son is the most appalling of goya's black paintings. saturn appears as a mad old man, eyes staring, mouth wide, both hands gripping a small body whose head and arm have already been bitten away. the background is black; only flesh and white cloth catch the light.\n\nin his late years goya shut himself in the quinta del sordo and painted these works directly onto the walls. they were neither commissions nor exhibition pieces, more like a private record of a man fighting fear. myth loses its allegory here and leaves only violence itself."], "auto-78b2a883": ["《教室》 the school room the school room 1820 1820 跨地域 作者不详（源站未著录） 学院素描 街巷 人间 跨地域 素描 维基共享资源 《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "the school room 1820 1820 cross-regional 作者不详（源站未著录） academic drawing streets human world cross-regional drawing wikimedia commons 1820, cross-regional. unknown; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:the school room - anon-c1820-70027.jpg. this is a drawing."], "constable-hay-wain-1821": ["《干草车》 1821 1821 欧洲 约翰·康斯太勃尔 浪漫主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《干草车》展示了一条浅河、一辆正在过河的干草车和一座农舍。左边是树木投下的阴影；右边天空突然开阔，云被吹散；车停在河中间，马儿在喝水，远处是萨福克的田野。\n\n康斯特布尔坚持户外作画，把英国的天气看作不断变化的状态，而不是背景。那座农舍是威利·洛特的小屋，他从小就认识这个地方。这种对当地土地的固执依恋，让风景画第一次具备了日常的分量。", "the hay wain 1821 1821 europe 约翰·康斯太勃尔 romanticism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the hay wain shows a shallow river, a hay wagon crossing it, and a farmhouse. trees cast shadow on the left; on the right the sky suddenly opens, clouds blown apart; the wagon stands midstream, horses drinking, suffolk fields beyond.\n\nconstable insisted on painting outdoors, treating english weather as a changing condition rather than a backdrop. the farmhouse is willy lott's cottage, a place he had known since childhood. this stubborn attachment to local ground gave landscape painting everyday weight for the first time."], "delacroix-liberty-1830": ["《自由引导人民》 1830 1830 欧洲 欧仁·德拉克罗瓦 浪漫主义 权利 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《自由引导人民》将1830年七月革命的路障变成了神话。自由女神站在中央，半裸着，右手举起三色旗，左手握着火枪，大踏步踩过尸体。她周围有戴高顶礼帽的市民、拿着手枪的青年、跪在地上的工人；背景是巴黎的屋顶和浓烟。\n\n德拉克洛瓦描绘革命时，不是井然有序的示威，而是混乱、血腥的进攻。三色旗是画面里最亮的颜色，就像一座灯塔，把人群吸引过去。这幅画后来成为法国共和国的象征之一。", "liberty leading the people 1830 1830 europe 欧仁·德拉克罗瓦 romanticism rights world affairs europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons liberty leading the people turns the barricades of the july revolution of 1830 into myth. liberty stands half-naked at the centre, the tricolour raised in her right hand, a musket in her left, striding over bodies. around her are a bourgeois in a top hat, a youth with pistols, a worker kneeling on the ground; paris rooftops and smoke behind.\n\ndelacroix paints the revolution not as an orderly demonstration but as a chaotic, bloody advance. the tricolour is the brightest colour in the picture, a lighthouse drawing the crowd towards it. the painting later became one of the symbols of the french republic."], "hokusai-south-wind-clear-sky-1831": ["《南风晴空》（赤富士） south wind, clear sky, from thirty-six views of mount fuji 1831 early 1830s 日本 江户 葛饰北斋 浮世绘 风景 天地 东亚 版画（彩色木刻） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 early 1830s，日本 江户。葛饰北斋的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "south wind, clear sky, from thirty-six views of mount fuji 1831 early 1830s 日本 江户 葛饰北斋 ukiyo-e landscape heaven and earth east asia 版画（彩色木刻） cleveland museum of art early 1830s, east asia. 葛饰北斋; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1930.189. this is a print (版画（彩色木刻）)."], "hokusai-great-wave-1831": ["《神奈川冲浪里》 1831 约1831 东亚 葛饰北斋 浮世绘 风景 天地 东亚 木版画 维基共享资源 《神奈川冲浪里》是葛饰北斋《富岳三十六景》中最著名的版画。一股巨大的海浪占据了画面：浪尖像爪子一样张开，三艘运输船被推到下面，船夫们低身躲避；远处的富士山几乎只是一个三角形，静静地停在浪的尽头。\n\n北斋用不同层次的普鲁士蓝印制海浪，从深靛蓝到浅白色，把海水切割成透明的刀锋。他在同一幅作品中展现了瞬间的暴力和永恒的宁静：浪会打下来，而富士山不会。", "the great wave off kanagawa 1831 约1831 east asia 葛饰北斋 ukiyo-e landscape heaven and earth east asia woodblock print wikimedia commons the great wave off kanagawa is the most famous print from hokusai's thirty-six views of mount fuji. an enormous wave dominates the sheet: its crest opens like talons, three transport boats are pushed beneath it, boatmen crouching low; far away mount fuji is almost only a triangle, resting quietly at the end of the wave.\n\nhokusai printed the wave in layers of prussian blue, from deep indigo to pale white, cutting the sea into translucent blades. he puts the violence of an instant and eternal stillness in one composition: the wave will fall, fuji will not."], "hiroshige-shono-driving-rain-1833": ["《庄野骤雨》 driving rain at shōno, from fifty-three stations of the tokaidō 1833 1833 日本 东海道 歌川广重 浮世绘 风景 天地 东亚 版画（彩色木刻） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1833，日本 东海道。歌川广重的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "driving rain at shōno, from fifty-three stations of the tokaidō 1833 1833 日本 东海道 歌川广重 ukiyo-e landscape heaven and earth east asia 版画（彩色木刻） cleveland museum of art 1833, east asia. 歌川广重; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1948.306. this is a print (版画（彩色木刻）)."], "turner-burning-houses-1835": ["《上下议院大火》 the burning of the houses of lords and commons, 16 october 1834 1835 1835 英国 伦敦 约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳 浪漫主义 灾变 世事 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1835，英国 伦敦。约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "the burning of the houses of lords and commons, 16 october 1834 1835 1835 london, united kingdom 约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳 romanticism disaster world affairs europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art 1835, europe. 约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·透纳; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1942.647. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "ingres-antiochus-stratonice-1838": ["《安条克与斯特拉托妮可》 antiochus and stratonice 1838 c. 1838 法国 巴黎 让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔 新古典主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（亚麻布） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1838，法国 巴黎。让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "antiochus and stratonice 1838 c. 1838 paris, france 让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔 neoclassicism faces human world europe 油画（亚麻布） cleveland museum of art c. 1838, europe. 让-奥古斯特-多米尼克·安格尔; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1966.13. this is a painting (油画（亚麻布）)."], "turner-fighting-temeraire-1839": ["《被拖去解体的无畏号》 1839 1839 欧洲 约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·特纳 浪漫主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《战斗的特梅莱尔号》描绘了一艘老战舰的最后航程。一艘拖船冒着黑烟，拖着白色的特梅莱尔号驶向拆船厂；夕阳西下，天空从金色逐渐变成深红色，水面像熔化的镜子。桅杆已不在，船身看起来空旷而巨大。\n\n特纳将工业与怀旧置于同一光线下：蒸汽拖船属于新时代，帆船则属于正在消逝的英国海上力量。美和哀悼在这里是同一个姿态，这也是这幅画成为英国最受喜爱的画作之一的原因。", "the fighting temeraire 1839 1839 europe 约瑟夫·马洛德·威廉·特纳 romanticism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the fighting temeraire depicts the last voyage of an old warship. a tug belches black smoke as it hauls the white temeraire towards the breaker's yard; the sun sets in the west, sky moving from gold to deep red, water like a molten mirror. the masts are gone, and the hull looks empty and enormous.\n\nturner puts industry and nostalgia into the same light: the steam tug belongs to the new age, the sailing ship to a vanishing british sea power. beauty and mourning are the same gesture here, which is why the picture became one of britain's best-loved paintings."], "aivazovsky-ninth-wave-1850": ["《九级浪》 1850 1850 欧洲 伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基 浪漫主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《第九波》描绘了风暴过后的黎明。海面上依然被巨浪撕裂；六个幸存者抓住浪尖上的一块残骸；天空从深蓝逐渐转为金橙色，阳光穿透了云层。中央的海浪像一堵透明的墙，几乎要吞没那些人。\n\n艾瓦佐夫斯基并未亲眼见过这场特定的风暴，但他画出了水的透明感、泡沫和折射，令人信服。他创作了数千幅海景画，其中这幅最为人引用：在一幅画里展现了大自然的力量和人类的渺小。", "the ninth wave 1850 1850 europe 伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基 romanticism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the ninth wave shows dawn after a storm. the sea is still torn by huge waves; six survivors cling to a piece of wreckage on the crest; the sky moves from deep blue to orange-gold as sunlight breaks through cloud. the central wave rises like a transparent wall, almost swallowing the figures.\n\naivazovsky had not witnessed this particular storm, yet he paints the transparency, foam and refraction of water with extraordinary conviction. he produced thousands of seascapes; this is the most quoted: nature's power and human smallness in one breath."], "auto-d713ad77": ["十九世纪英国学校教室 classroom 19th century english school a nineteenth-century english classroom 1850 1850 欧洲 作者不详（源站未著录） 风俗画 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画 维基共享资源 《十九世纪英国学校教室》是佚名画家约1850年的风俗画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“十九世纪英国学校教室”为题，属于英国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "a nineteenth-century english classroom 1850 1850 europe 作者不详（源站未著录） genre painting streets human world europe oil painting wikimedia commons 1850, europe. unknown; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:classroom 19th century english school.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "courbet-painters-studio-1855": ["《画室》 1855 1855 欧洲 居斯塔夫·库尔贝 现实主义 劳作 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《画家的工作室》的副标题是“一个真正的寓言，总结了我七年的艺术和道德生活”。在画面中央，库尔贝坐在画架前画风景画，旁边有裸体模特和一个男孩。右边是他的朋友和支持者——波德莱尔、普鲁东、尚弗勒里等；左边是日常生活中的普通人：工人、农民、乞丐、一位寡妇。库尔贝把“社会”搬进了画室，把艺术创作和政治立场放在同一个空间里。这既是对学院派的挑战，也是现实主义宣言：画家不画神话，而是画他眼中的人。", "the painter's studio 1855 1855 europe 居斯塔夫·库尔贝 realism work human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the painter's studio carries the subtitle \"a real allegory summing up seven years of my artistic and moral life.\" at the centre, courbet sits at his easel painting a landscape, a nude model and a boy beside him. on the right are his friends and supporters — baudelaire, proudhon, champfleury and others; on the left, ordinary people from daily life: workers, peasants, beggars, a widow.\n\ncourbet moves \"society\" into the studio and puts artistic production and political stance in the same room. it is both a challenge to the academy and a realist manifesto: the painter does not paint myth, but the people he sees."], "hiroshige-sudden-shower-1857": ["《大桥骤雨》 1857 1857 东亚 歌川广重 浮世绘 风景 天地 东亚 木版画 维基共享资源 《大桥与安宅的骤雨》描绘了一个木桥横跨隅田川的景象，在暴雨中行人匆匆而过：有人撑伞，有人缩着肩膀，有人干脆淋湿。雨水被画成密集的斜线；河流、屋顶和远岸被压平为灰蓝色的轮廓。\n\n广重没有画暴风雨的中心，而是描绘雨点打在人们身上的瞬间。这样的斜线节奏吸引了梵高，他用油画临摹了这幅版画，把雨画成厚厚的颜料笔触。", "sudden shower over shin-ōhashi bridge and atake 1857 1857 east asia 歌川广重 ukiyo-e landscape heaven and earth east asia woodblock print wikimedia commons sudden shower over shin-ōhashi bridge and atake shows a wooden bridge over the sumida river as a rainstorm drives pedestrians across it: some open umbrellas, some hunch their shoulders, some simply get wet. rain is cut as dense diagonal lines; river, roofs and the far bank are flattened into grey-blue silhouettes.\n\nhiroshige does not paint the storm's centre but the moment rain lands on people. that rhythm of diagonals fascinated van gogh, who copied the print in oil, turning the rain into thick strokes of paint."], "millet-the-gleaners-1857": ["《拾穗者》 1857 1857 欧洲 让-弗朗索瓦·米勒 现实主义 劳作 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《拾穗者》展示了三个农妇在收割后弯腰捡拾散落的谷粒。她们的身体几乎折成直角，手触地面；她们身后是干草堆、收割工人和淡金色的天空。画面没有故事，只有反复的劳作和沉重的地平线。\n\n米勒赋予了他那个时代最不被重视的劳动以宏大的规模：三个形象就像低矮的雕塑，沉默、稳固，不需要同情。当时的保守评论家看作这是危险的宣言，因为它赋予了贫困以尊严和份量。", "the gleaners 1857 1857 europe 让-弗朗索瓦·米勒 realism work human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the gleaners shows three peasant women bending to pick up scattered grain after the harvest. their bodies fold almost to the right angle, hands reaching the ground; behind them stand haystacks, harvesters and a pale gold sky. there is no story, only repeated labour and a heavy horizon.\n\nmillet gives the least regarded work of his time a monumental scale: three figures like low sculptures, silent, solid, asking for no pity. conservative critics read it as a dangerous manifesto when it was shown, because it gave poverty dignity and volume."], "manet-olympia-1863": ["《奥林匹亚》 1863 1863 欧洲 爱德华·马奈 现实主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《奥林匹亚》用19世纪巴黎的现实取代了提香式的躺卧裸女。奥林匹亚穿着拖鞋和黑丝带躺在床上，直视观者；她身后，一名黑人女仆手捧花束，一只黑猫站在她脚边，尾巴竖起。床、花束和披肩的描绘平直直接，没有古典的柔和感。\n\n这幅画在1865年沙龙展引起了轰动：问题不在于裸体，而在于她的目光。她不再是被观看的对象，而是会回望的人。马奈的平涂和强烈的黑白对比打破了自文艺复兴以来统治裸体画的观赏规则。", "olympia 1863 1863 europe 爱德华·马奈 realism faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons olympia replaces the titianesque reclining nude with the reality of nineteenth-century paris. olympia lies on a bed in slippers and a black ribbon, looking directly at the viewer; behind her a black maid holds flowers, and a black cat stands at her feet, tail up. bed, bouquet and shawl are painted flatly and directly, without classical softness.\n\nthe painting caused a scandal at the 1865 salon: the problem was not nudity but her gaze. she is no longer an object to be looked at but someone who looks back. manet's flat paint and hard black-white contrasts break the viewing contract that had governed the nude since the renaissance."], "manet-dejeuner-sur-herbe-1863": ["《草地上的午餐》 1863 1863 欧洲 爱德华·马奈 现实主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《草地上的午餐》把一个裸体女人和两个完全穿着的男人放在巴黎郊外的草地上。女人坐在左边，膝盖弯起，目光直视画外；男人们在聊天，似乎毫不在意。另一名女子在后面的溪边弯腰。光透过树叶洒下，人物看起来像是贴在同一个平面上。\n\n马奈借鉴了乔尔乔内《田园音乐会》的构图，但去掉了神话和田园诗意。裸体不再是女神，只是一个在午餐的巴黎女性；这种莫名其妙的并置使这幅画成为现代艺术最早的丑闻之一。", "le déjeuner sur l'herbe 1863 1863 europe 爱德华·马奈 realism faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons le déjeuner sur l'herbe places a nude woman and two fully dressed men on grass outside paris. the woman sits at the left, knees drawn up, looking straight out of the picture; the men talk, apparently unconcerned. another woman bends by the stream behind. light falls through leaves, and the figures seem pasted onto a single plane.\n\nmanet borrows the composition of giorgione's pastoral concert but removes myth and idyll. the nude is no longer a goddess, only a parisian woman at lunch; this unexplained juxtaposition made the painting one of the first scandals of modern art."], "auto-9afb2e56": ["老妇肖像 portrait of an old woman lacma 83.1.13 portrait of an old woman 1865 1865 跨地域 wilhelm leibl (germany, cologne, 1844-1900) 现实主义 面孔 人间 跨地域 版画 维基共享资源 《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "portrait of an old woman 1865 1865 cross-regional wilhelm leibl (germany, cologne, 1844-1900) realism faces human world cross-regional print wikimedia commons 1865, cross-regional. 威廉·莱布尔; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:portrait of an old woman lacma 83.1.1354c.jpg. this is a print."], "monet-red-kerchief-1870": ["《红围巾》 the red kerchief 1870 c. 1868–73 法国 克劳德·莫奈 印象主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 c. 1868–73，法国。克劳德·莫奈的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "the red kerchief 1870 c. 1868–73 france 克劳德·莫奈 impressionism faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art c. 1868–73, europe. 克劳德·莫奈; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1958.39. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "whistler-arrangement-grey-black-1871": ["《灰与黑的协奏曲：画家母亲肖像》 1871 1871 北美 詹姆斯·麦克尼尔·惠斯勒 唯美主义 面孔 人间 北美 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《灰与黑的安排》第一号展示了一位老妇人侧身坐着，脚下放着一只脚凳；她穿着黑色连衣裙和白色帽子，背景是灰色的墙和几幅装裱的画作。画中几乎没有故事，只有垂直和水平的线条以及黑色和灰色的层次。\n\n惠斯勒坚持用音乐式的标题，拒绝让这幅画被解读为“母亲”或“肖像”。他想要一种安排：色彩、形状和情绪像乐谱一样构成。这种唯美主义态度后来影响了抽象艺术对绘画本身的关注。", "arrangement in grey and black no. 1 1871 1871 north america 詹姆斯·麦克尼尔·惠斯勒 aestheticism faces human world north america oil on canvas wikimedia commons arrangement in grey and black no. 1 shows an elderly woman seated in profile, a footstool at her feet; she wears a black dress and white cap, against a grey wall and a few framed prints. there is almost no story, only vertical and horizontal lines and a scale of black and grey.\n\nwhistler insisted on musical titles and refused to let the picture be read as \"mother\" or \"portrait.\" he wanted an arrangement: colour, shape and mood composed like a score. this aestheticist attitude later shaped abstract art's attention to painting itself."], "monet-impression-sunrise-1872": ["《印象·日出》 1872 1872 欧洲 克劳德·莫奈 印象主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《印象·日出》展示了勒阿弗尔港的黎明。太阳是一个橘红色的小点；薄雾把水面分成灰蓝色和浅紫色；远处的吊车、烟囱和桅杆都模糊不清，而前景中一只小船用几笔短刷划破水面。\n\n莫奈不画轮廓，他记录的是某一瞬间空气中的光。评论家路易·勒鲁瓦借用这个标题来讽刺这些画家为“印象派”，这个名字最终被画家们接受。现代绘画的名字就这样因为误解而产生了。", "impression, sunrise 1872 1872 europe 克劳德·莫奈 impressionism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons impression, sunrise shows dawn in the port of le havre. the sun is an orange-red dot; mist divides the water into grey-blue and pale violet; cranes, chimneys and masts blur in the distance, while a small boat cuts the surface in the foreground with a few short strokes.\n\nmonet does not draw outlines; he records light in the air at a particular moment. the critic louis leroy borrowed the title to mock these painters as \"impressionists,\" and the name was taken up by the group. modern painting acquired its name through a misreading."], "morisot-the-cradle-1872": ["《摇篮》 1872 1872 欧洲 贝尔特·莫里索 印象主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《摇篮》展示了画家的妹妹埃德玛坐在婴儿床旁，通过纱帘看着熟睡的宝宝。她用左臂支撑着头，右手放在婴儿床边；面纱像薄雾一样覆盖在孩子的脸上。灰色、浅蓝色和粉色为主，轮廓几乎消失。\n\n莫里索是印象派中最重要的女性，她画的不是公共空间的景象，而是家庭的宁静内部。观看的姿态温柔，但也略显疲惫和恍惚。", "the cradle 1872 1872 europe 贝尔特·莫里索 impressionism faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the cradle shows the painter's sister edma seated beside a cot, watching her sleeping baby through a gauze curtain. her left arm supports her head, her right hand rests on the cot's edge; the veil lies over the child's face like mist. greys, pale blues and pinks dominate, and outlines are almost absent.\n\nmorisot was the most important woman in the impressionist group, and she painted not the spectacle of public space but the quiet interior of the family. the pose of watching is tender, but also a little tired and absent."], "repin-barge-haulers-1873": ["《伏尔加河上的纤夫》 1873 1870–1873 欧洲 伊利亚·列宾 现实主义 劳作 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《伏尔加河上的驳船拉夫》展示了一支由十一人组成的队伍沿河拉绳，身体前倾，双脚陷入沙中。前面一位老人目视前方；他身后的一位年轻人试图抬起头。宽阔的河流、远处的小船和炽热的天空在他们身后展开。\n\n作为学生的列宾曾沿伏尔加河旅行，并在看到这些拉夫后开始创作这幅画。他把俄罗斯的贫困和坚韧转化为一种影像。", "barge haulers on the volga 1873 1870–1873 europe 伊利亚·列宾 realism work human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons barge haulers on the volga shows a team of eleven men hauling a rope along the river, bodies leaning forward, feet sunk in sand. at the front an old man stares ahead; behind him a younger man tries to lift his head. the broad river, a distant boat and a hot sky lie behind them.\n\nas a student repin travelled the volga and began the picture after seeing the haulers. he turns russian poverty and endurance into a physical epic: no heroes, only people joined by a rope."], "degas-dance-class-1874": ["《舞蹈课》 1874 1873–1876 欧洲 埃德加·德加 印象主义 劳作 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《舞蹈课》展示了巴黎歌剧院芭蕾舞的排练室。中央，一位年长的芭蕾舞导师靠着一根长杖，指导一群穿着白色芭蕾舞裙的女孩；有些在认真听讲，有些在挠背、整理肩带或者发呆。对角线划分了整个房间，镜子、钢琴和地板又把空间向后推。\n\n德加并不追求舞台上的完美，而是展现排练中的疲惫、等待和小动作。他受英格尔风格素描训练，用类似粉彩的色彩和不对称的构图，把幕后世界变成现代绘画的真正主题。", "the dance class 1874 1873–1876 europe 埃德加·德加 impressionism work human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the dance class shows a rehearsal room of the paris opéra ballet. at the centre an elderly ballet master leans on a long staff, addressing a group of girls in white tutus; some listen, others scratch their backs, adjust a shoulder strap or drift off. a diagonal cuts the room, and mirror, piano and floor push the space back.\n\ndegas does not seek stage perfection but the fatigue, waiting and small gestures of rehearsal. trained in ingresque drawing, he uses pastel-like colour and asymmetric composition to make the backstage the proper subject of modern painting."], "renoir-bal-moulin-galette-1876": ["《煎饼磨坊的舞会》 1876 1876 欧洲 皮埃尔-奥古斯特·雷诺阿 印象主义 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《加莱特磨坊的舞会》描绘了蒙马特高地上一场夏天的露天舞会。人群在树影和阳光间穿梭；前景的桌旁有人坐着聊天，而舞者则在中心旋转。树叶将光线分割成片，洒落在衣服、帽子和脸上。\n\n雷诺阿画的不是孤立的人物，而是人群之间的空气：笑声、汗水、香水、烟草和阴影混合在一起。这既是印象派画作中最欢乐的一幅，也是十九世纪巴黎休闲生活的视觉记录。", "bal du moulin de la galette 1876 1876 europe 皮埃尔-奥古斯特·雷诺阿 impressionism streets human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons bal du moulin de la galette shows a summer dance in the open air on the montmartre hill. crowds move between tree shadow and sunlight; at a table in the foreground people sit and talk, while dancers turn at the centre. leaves cut the light into fragments that fall across clothes, hats and faces.\n\nrenoir paints not isolated figures but the air between people: laughter, sweat, perfume, tobacco and shade mixed together. it is both the most joyful of impressionist paintings and a visual record of nineteenth-century parisian leisure."], "manet-bar-folies-bergere-1882": ["《女神游乐厅的吧台》 1882 1882 欧洲 爱德华·马奈 现实主义 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《福乐喜剧酒吧》展示了巴黎音乐厅的最后一夜。一个酒吧女侍站在柜台后，双手放在大理石台面上，胸前别着一朵花；她面前摆着酒杯、酒瓶和一盘橘子。她身后的镜子反射出整个大厅：吊灯、观众、包厢，以及一个正和她交谈的男人——这也是观众实际上所处的位置。\n\n马奈画的反射并不完全正确，透视也略有偏差。酒吧女侍的表情空洞，既不欢迎也不拒绝。整幅画成为现代城市生活的标志性形象：人群、光线、消费，以及一个无法接近的人。", "a bar at the folies-bergère 1882 1882 europe 爱德华·马奈 realism streets human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons a bar at the folies-bergère shows the last night of a paris music hall. a barmaid stands behind the counter, both hands resting on the marble, a flower at her breast; glasses, bottles and a plate of oranges are arranged in front of her. the mirror behind her reflects the whole hall: chandeliers, audience, boxes, and a man speaking to her — the place where the viewer actually stands.\n\nmanet paints the reflection not quite correctly and lets the perspective slip. the barmaid's expression is blank, neither welcoming nor refusing. the picture becomes a defining image of modern city life: crowd, light, consumption, and a person who cannot be reached."], "boecklin-isle-of-the-dead-1883": ["《死之岛》 1883 1883 欧洲 阿诺德·勃克林 象征主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《死之岛》展示了一个漂浮在海上的墓地：一个被黑色柏树覆盖的岩石岛屿，垂直升起的悬崖；一只小船靠近码头，船上站着一个穿白衣的人，船首放着一口棺材。天空灰蓝沉重，水面几乎静止。\n\n伯克林并没有画特定的地中海岛屿；他把死亡变成了一种空间——一个既无法抵达也无法离开的岛屿。它被无数次模仿和改编，并影响了二十世纪梦境和电影的视觉形象。", "isle of the dead 1883 1883 europe 阿诺德·勃克林 symbolism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons isle of the dead shows a cemetery floating on the sea: a rocky island covered with dark cypresses, cliffs rising vertically; a small boat approaches the landing, a figure in white standing aboard, a coffin at the bow. the sky is a heavy grey-blue, the water almost still.\n\nböcklin does not paint a specific mediterranean island; he turns death into a space — an island that can be neither reached nor left. it was copied and adapted endlessly, and shaped twentieth-century images of dream and film."], "sargent-madame-x-1884": ["《x夫人》 1884 1883–1884 北美 约翰·辛格·萨金特 肖像画·学院之外 面孔 人间 北美 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《x女士》描绘的是维珍妮·阿梅莉·阿韦尼奥·戈特罗，一位著名的巴黎美女。她侧身站立，一只手搭在桌子上，头向后仰，露出一张苍白的脸和鼻子；她黑色缎面礼服的肩带滑落，肌肤与布料形成冷峻的对比。这幅画在1884年的沙龙展引起了轰动：不是因为裸露，而是因为姿态太自傲、太不受控制。萨金特后来重新画了肩带，但这种挑衅感并没有消失。它仍然是19世纪末“新女性”最尖锐的肖像之一。", "madame x (madame pierre gautreau) 1884 1883–1884 north america 约翰·辛格·萨金特 portraiture beyond the academy faces human world north america oil on canvas wikimedia commons madame x portrays virginie amélie avegno gautreau, a celebrated parisian beauty. she stands in profile, one hand resting on a table, her head thrown back to reveal a pale face and nose; the strap of her black satin dress has slipped, skin and fabric set in cold contrast.\n\nthe picture caused a scandal at the 1884 salon: not for nudity but for a posture too proud, too ungovernable. sargent later repainted the strap, yet the provocation did not disappear. it remains one of the sharpest portraits of the late-nineteenth-century \"new woman.\""], "auto-0d3092e4": ["祖母 iii anders zorn - grandmother iii (1884) grandmother iii 1884 1884 跨地域 anders zorn 现实主义 面孔 人间 跨地域 版画 维基共享资源 《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "grandmother iii 1884 1884 cross-regional anders zorn realism faces human world cross-regional print wikimedia commons 1884, cross-regional. 安德斯·佐恩; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:anders zorn - grandmother iii 1884 - bukowskis lot no. 534975.jpg. this is a print."], "auto-e13d5cd2": ["里约港 giovanni battista castagneto - porto do rio de janeiro, 1884 port of rio de janeiro 1884 1884 中南美 giovanni battista castagneto 印象主义 风景 天地 中南美 油画 维基共享资源 《里约港》是乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托约1884年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约港”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "port of rio de janeiro 1884 1884 latin america giovanni battista castagneto impressionism landscape heaven and earth latin america oil painting wikimedia commons 1884, latin america. 乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:giovanni battista castagneto - porto do rio de janeiro, 1884.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-ba3dba36": ["里约港（其二） giovanni battista castagneto - porto do rio de janeiro (2) port of rio de janeiro ii 1884 1884 中南美 giovanni battista castagneto 印象主义 风景 天地 中南美 油画 维基共享资源 《里约港（其二）》是乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托约1884年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约港（其二）”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "port of rio de janeiro ii 1884 1884 latin america giovanni battista castagneto impressionism landscape heaven and earth latin america oil painting wikimedia commons 1884, latin america. 乔瓦尼·巴蒂斯塔·卡斯塔涅托; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:giovanni battista castagneto - porto do rio de janeiro (2).jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-723f2014": ["里约热内卢罗德里戈湖 nicola facchinetti - lagoa rodrigo de freitas, rio de janeiro, ca. 1884 lagoa rodrigo de freitas, rio de janeiro 1884 1884 中南美 nicola antonio facchinetti 学院派风景 风景 天地 中南美 油画 维基共享资源 《里约热内卢罗德里戈湖》是尼古拉·法基内蒂约1884年的学院派风景作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约热内卢罗德里戈湖”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "lagoa rodrigo de freitas, rio de janeiro 1884 1884 latin america nicola antonio facchinetti academic landscape landscape heaven and earth latin america oil painting wikimedia commons 1884, latin america. 尼古拉·法基内蒂; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:nicola facchinetti - lagoa rodrigo de freitas, rio de janeiro, ca. 1884.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-ad61b00e": ["里约全景习作：蛇岛 victor meirelles - estudo para panorama do rio de janeiro e morro de santo antônio, c. 1885 study for panorama of rio de janeiro: ilha das cobras and morro de santo antônio 1885 1885 中南美 victor meirelles 学院派 风景 天地 中南美 油画 维基共享资源 《里约全景习作：蛇岛》是维克托·梅雷莱斯约1885年的学院派作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“里约全景习作：蛇岛”为题，属于巴西的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "study for panorama of rio de janeiro: ilha das cobras and morro de santo antônio 1885 1885 latin america victor meirelles academic painting landscape heaven and earth latin america oil painting wikimedia commons 1885, latin america. 维克托·梅雷莱斯; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:victor meirelles - estudo para panorama do rio de janeiro - ilha das cobras e morro de santo antônio - c. 1885.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "seurat-grande-jatte-1886": ["《大碗岛的星期天下午》 1886 1884–1886 欧洲 乔治·修拉 后印象主义 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《拉格朗德岛的一个星期天》展示了塞纳河边的公园：人们坐在草地上，撑着阳伞，遛狗，划船，所有人都像暂停动作的剪影。画面由无数小色点组成；远看是统一的绿色和蓝色，近看则是橙色、紫色和黄色的小颗粒。人物被简化为纵横的块状，连影子都像用尺子量过一样。\n\n苏拉将色彩科学、光学理论和古典构图融合到一幅画中。它延续了印象派对光线的兴趣，却又与印象派的“瞬间感”相反：这里的一切都是静止且可计算的，是现代城市生活的一个样本。", "a sunday on la grande jatte 1886 1884–1886 europe 乔治·修拉 post-impressionism streets human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons a sunday on la grande jatte shows a park beside the seine: people sit on grass, hold parasols, walk dogs, row boats, all like silhouettes paused mid-motion. the surface is built from countless small dots of colour; from a distance they read as unified green and blue, up close as grains of orange, violet and yellow. figures are reduced to vertical and horizontal blocks, even shadows measured as if by ruler.\n\nseurat brings colour science, optical theory and classical composition into one picture. it extends impressionism's interest in light and contradicts its \"instant\": everything here is still and calculable, a specimen of modern city life."], "auto-aed4a918": ["黑海海岸沉船 ivan konstantinovich aivazovsky - shipwreck off the black sea coast shipwreck off the black sea coast 1887 1887 跨地域 ivan aivazovsky 浪漫主义 灾变 世事 跨地域 油画 维基共享资源 《黑海海岸沉船》是伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基约1887年的浪漫主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“黑海海岸沉船”为题，属于黑海的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "shipwreck off the black sea coast 1887 1887 cross-regional ivan aivazovsky romanticism disaster world affairs cross-regional oil painting wikimedia commons 1887, cross-regional. 伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:ivan konstantinovich aivazovsky - shipwreck off the black sea coast.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "van-gogh-sunflowers-1888": ["《向日葵》 1888 1888 欧洲 文森特·梵高 后印象主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《向日葵》展示了阿尔勒黄色房子里的一个花瓶。花朵从明亮的金色到焦棕色不等，花瓣烫焦；背景是一片同样明亮的黄色，花瓶下方只有一条青绿色的线。颜料厚重，几乎从画布上凸起。\n\n梵高计划这组作品是为了在高更到来时装饰黄色房子。对他来说，黄色不是一种颜色，而是一种温度，一种友谊的承诺，以及几乎宗教般的光。", "sunflowers 1888 1888 europe 文森特·梵高 post-impressionism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons sunflowers shows a vase in the yellow house at arles. the flower heads move from bright gold to burnt brown, petals singed; the background is a field of the same luminous yellow, with only a line of green-blue below the vase. paint is thick, almost standing off the canvas.\n\nvan gogh planned this series to decorate the yellow house for gauguin's arrival. for him yellow was not a colour but a temperature, a promise of friendship, and an almost religious light."], "van-gogh-starry-night-1889": ["《星月夜》 1889 1889 欧洲 文森特·梵高 后印象主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《星月夜》是在圣雷米的精神病院创作的。天空像漩涡一样旋转，星星像火球般燃烧，月亮在右侧升起；前景的一棵柏树像黑色火焰一样升起；下面是一个宁静的村庄，教堂的尖塔指向远方。\n\n梵高并不是仅凭记忆绘制这片天空；他把窗外的景色与想象和内心的波动结合在一起。厚重、明显的笔触让画面既有运动感又有静止感：世界在转动，而观者固定在窗前。", "the starry night 1889 1889 europe 文森特·梵高 post-impressionism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the starry night was painted at the asylum in saint-rémy. the sky becomes a swirling vortex, stars burning like fireballs, the moon rising at the right; a cypress in the foreground rises like a black flame; below lies a quiet village, its church spire pointing into the distance.\n\nvan gogh did not paint this sky from memory alone; he mixed the view from his window with imagination and inner turbulence. the thick, visible strokes give the picture both motion and stasis: the world turns, while the viewer is fixed at the window."], "auto-dd7aafa6": ["开罗街景（蚀刻版画） marius bauer - a street in cairo (etching) a street in cairo (etching) 1890 1890 西亚·北非 marius bauer 象征主义 街巷 人间 西亚·北非 版画 维基共享资源 《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "a street in cairo (etching) 1890 1890 west asia & north africa marius bauer symbolism streets human world west asia & north africa print wikimedia commons 1890, west asia & north africa. 马里乌斯·鲍尔; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:marius bauer.'a street in cairo'.etching on paper,28.5cm х 23.1cm.jpg. this is a print."], "munch-the-scream-1893": ["《呐喊》 1893 1893 欧洲 爱德华·蒙克 象征主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 蛋彩与油彩（纸板） 维基共享资源 《呐喊》展示了奥斯陆峡湾旁的一座桥。中央人物捂着耳朵，嘴巴张开，脸扭曲得像骷髅一样；在他身后，天空呈现橙红色的条纹，水是深蓝色的，两个人影朝远处走去。栏杆在画面中划出一条斜线，仿佛观者也被推向前去。\n\n在日记中，蒙克描述自己听到了“来自大自然的巨大、无限的尖叫”。这并不是一个人在尖叫，而是环境对一个人施加的压力。这幅画成为现代焦虑的普遍象征，被无数次模仿和恶搞，但仍然很有冲击力。", "the scream 1893 1893 europe 爱德华·蒙克 symbolism faces human world europe tempera and oil on board wikimedia commons the scream shows a bridge beside the oslo fjord. the central figure covers his ears, mouth open, face twisted like a skull; behind him the sky turns in orange-red bands, water is deep blue, and two dark figures walk away. the railing cuts a diagonal out of the picture, as if the viewer were being pushed forward too.\n\nin his diary munch described hearing \"a great, infinite scream from nature.\" it is not a person screaming so much as an environment pressing on one person. the image became the universal sign of modern anxiety, copied and parodied countless times, and still effective."], "moreau-jupiter-semele-1895": ["《朱庇特与塞墨勒》 1895 1895 欧洲 居斯塔夫·莫罗 象征主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《朱庇特与塞墨勒》展示了凡人塞墨勒要求看到神以真实形态的瞬间。朱庇特坐在中央的宝座上，一条巨蛇盘在胸前，周围环绕着层层金色装饰和神祇；塞墨勒斜卧在前景，她的身体已经被神圣之光穿透，几乎在溶解。莫罗将神话描绘成一个象征的宫殿：色彩如搪瓷，线条似珠宝，没有深度，只有无尽的装饰。这里的象征主义不是讲故事；画面本身成为一个迷宫，眼睛可以一次又一次地进入。", "jupiter and semele 1895 1895 europe 居斯塔夫·莫罗 symbolism faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons jupiter and semele shows the moment the mortal semele asks to see the god in his true form. jupiter sits on a throne at the centre, a great serpent coiled at his breast, surrounded by tiers of gold ornament and deities; semele reclines in the foreground, her body already pierced by divine light, almost dissolving.\n\nmoreau paints myth as a palace of symbols: colour like enamel, line like jewellery, no depth, only endless ornament. symbolism here is not storytelling; the image itself becomes a labyrinth the eye can enter again and again."], "auto-e80436fe": ["暴风雨早晨的沉船 ivan konstantinovich aivazovsky - shipwreck on a stormy morning, 1895 shipwreck on a stormy morning 1895 1895 跨地域 ivan aivazovsky 浪漫主义 灾变 世事 跨地域 油画 维基共享资源 《暴风雨早晨的沉船》是伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基约1895年的浪漫主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“暴风雨早晨的沉船”为题，属于黑海的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "shipwreck on a stormy morning 1895 1895 cross-regional ivan aivazovsky romanticism disaster world affairs cross-regional oil painting wikimedia commons 1895, cross-regional. 伊凡·艾瓦佐夫斯基; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:ivan konstantinovich aivazovsky - shipwreck on a stormy morning, 1895.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "munch-evening-melancholy-1896": ["《傍晚的忧郁 i》 evening, melancholy i 1896 1896 挪威 奥斯陆 爱德华·蒙克 表现主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 版画（手工上色木刻） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1896，挪威 奥斯陆。爱德华·蒙克的版画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件版画作品，线条与印痕记录了图像被复制的路径。", "evening, melancholy i 1896 1896 挪威 奥斯陆 爱德华·蒙克 expressionism faces human world europe 版画（手工上色木刻） cleveland museum of art 1896, europe. 爱德华·蒙克; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1959.82. this is a print (版画（手工上色木刻）)."], "pissarro-boulevard-montmartre-night-1897": ["《蒙马特大道·夜色》 1897 1897 欧洲 卡米耶·毕沙罗 印象主义 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《蒙马特大街夜景》是皮萨罗的一系列作品之一，他从巴黎一家酒店的窗口俯视街道。大街斜向右延伸，路灯将湿漉漉的柏油路照成金色的线条；马车、行人和商店橱窗被压缩成短短的笔触。天空深蓝，建筑物是黑色的剪影。\n\n晚年的皮萨罗遭受眼疾困扰，但在这组城市题材作品中找到了新的自由：他不再画乡村风景，而是描绘现代城市的节奏与光影。印象派的“瞬间”变成了大都市的夜脉动。", "the boulevard montmartre at night 1897 1897 europe 卡米耶·毕沙罗 impressionism streets human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons the boulevard montmartre at night is one of a series pissarro painted looking down on the street from a paris hotel window. the boulevard runs diagonally away to the right, streetlamps turning wet asphalt into lines of gold; carriages, pedestrians and shop windows are compressed into short strokes. the sky is deep blue, the buildings black silhouettes.\n\npissarro was troubled by eye disease in his late years, yet found a new freedom in this urban series: he no longer painted the countryside but the rhythm and light of the modern city. the impressionist \"instant\" becomes the night pulse of a metropolis."], "gauguin-where-do-we-come-from-1898": ["《我们从何处来？我们是谁？我们向何处去？》 1898 1897–1898 大洋洲 保罗·高更 后印象主义 面孔 人间 大洋洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《我们从何处来？我们是谁？我们向何处去？》是高更塔希提时期最大的画作。画面的构图是从右向左阅读的——婴儿、女人、老人——就像一个无字的创世纪。中央人物伸手去拿水果，周围是蓝色和绿色的阴影；背后是大海、山脉和神龛。画名刻在左下角，就像墙上的墓志铭。\n\n高更并不是在讲一个具体的故事，而是用身体、色彩和符号拼凑出三个问题。他把殖民地的“他处”变成一个哲学空间，并把自己的焦虑隐藏在那些静止、几乎像雕塑的形象里。", "where do we come from? what are we? where are we going? 1898 1897–1898 oceania 保罗·高更 post-impressionism faces human world oceania oil on canvas wikimedia commons where do we come from? what are we? where are we going? is gauguin's largest painting from his tahiti years. the composition reads from right to left — infant, woman, old person — like a genesis without words. a central figure reaches for fruit, surrounded by blue and green shadow; sea, mountains and a shrine lie behind. the title is inscribed at the lower left like an epitaph on a wall.\n\ngauguin is not telling a specific story but assembling three questions from bodies, colour and symbol. he turns the colonial \"elsewhere\" into a philosophical space, and hides his own anxiety inside those still, almost sculptural figures."], "cezanne-the-brook-1898": ["《溪流》 the brook 1898 c. 1895–1900 法国 普罗旺斯 保罗·塞尚 后印象主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 塞尚把溪流、岩石和树处理成同一套笔触；水不是倒影，而是另一组倾斜的色块。", "the brook 1898 c. 1895–1900 法国 普罗旺斯 保罗·塞尚 post-impressionism landscape heaven and earth europe oil painting cleveland museum of art c. 1895–1900, europe. 保罗·塞尚; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1958.2. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "oerder-still-life-1900": ["《静物》 still-life 1900 1900 南非 比勒陀利亚 弗兰斯·奥尔德 南非静物画 痕迹 技艺 撒哈拉以南非洲 油画 维基共享资源 奥尔德1900年的静物把器物摆成一座小型舞台；桌面的反光比物件本身更先被看见。", "still-life 1900 1900 南非 比勒陀利亚 弗兰斯·奥尔德 south african still life traces craft sub-saharan africa oil painting wikimedia commons 1900, sub-saharan africa. 弗兰斯·奥尔德; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. frans oerder - still-life - google art project.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-62ae36e0": ["从克洛夫街高处看开普敦 heinrich hermann - cape town from the top of kloof street cape town from the top of kloof street 1900 1900 撒哈拉以南非洲 heinrich hermann (1842 - 1916) 殖民地地形水彩 风景 天地 撒哈拉以南非洲 水彩 维基共享资源 《从克洛夫街高处看开普敦》是海因里希·赫尔曼约1900年的殖民地地形水彩作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“从克洛夫街高处看开普敦”为题，属于开普敦的水彩传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "cape town from the top of kloof street 1900 1900 sub-saharan africa heinrich hermann (1842 - 1916) colonial topographical watercolour landscape heaven and earth sub-saharan africa watercolour wikimedia commons 1900, sub-saharan africa. 海因里希·赫尔曼; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:heinrich hermann - cape town from the top of kloof street - google art project.jpg. this is a painting (watercolour)."], "auto-580fb4aa": ["列夫·托尔斯泰肖像 leo tolstoy by i.s. kazakov (1900, odessa) leo tolstoy 1900 1900 欧洲 ivan kazakov 现实主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 绘画 维基共享资源 《列夫·托尔斯泰肖像》是伊万·卡扎科夫约1900年的现实主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“列夫·托尔斯泰肖像”为题，属于俄国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "leo tolstoy 1900 1900 europe ivan kazakov realism faces human world europe painting wikimedia commons 1900, europe. 伊万·卡扎科夫; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:leo tolstoy by i.s.kazakov (1900, odessa).jpg. this is a painting."], "auto-27bcc7d5": ["咖啡壶静物 camille pissarro, still life with a coffeepot still life with a coffeepot 1900 1900 欧洲 camille pissarro 印象主义 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 绘画 维基共享资源 《咖啡壶静物》是卡米耶·毕沙罗约1900年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“咖啡壶静物”为题，属于法国的绘画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "still life with a coffeepot 1900 1900 europe camille pissarro impressionism traces craft europe painting wikimedia commons 1900, europe. 卡米耶·毕沙罗; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:camille pissarro, still life with a coffeepot, 1900, зкрсэ-527, hermitage museum.jpg. this is a painting."], "auto-9fd3fc18": ["比利·梅森 anders zorn - billy mason (1900) billy mason 1900 1900 大洋洲 anders zorn 现实主义 面孔 人间 大洋洲 版画 维基共享资源 《女史箴图》是现存最早的中国绢本人物长卷之一，通常被认为是东晋顾恺之的原作、唐代摹本。画卷根据张华《女史箴》的十二段箴文绘制，现存九段：有冯媛挡熊、班姬辞辇，也有宫中女子对镜梳妆、围坐交谈的日常场景。人物衣带飘举，线条细而不断，像春蚕吐丝。\n\n画面没有透视，也没有阴影，却用线条的节奏、人物之间的距离和空白来组织叙事。它既是道德教科书，也是一部宫廷女性生活的图像史。1900年庚子事变后流入英国，现藏大英博物馆。", "billy mason 1900 1900 oceania anders zorn realism faces human world oceania print wikimedia commons 1900, oceania. 安德斯·佐恩; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:anders zorn - billy mason 1900 - museum of new zealand 1971-0012-48.jpg. this is a print."], "auto-58575fef": ["湄公河上的“安南号” vilhelm arnesen - dampskibet annam på mekongfloden ved saigon - 1900 the steamer annam on the mekong near saigon 1900 1900 东南亚 vilhelm arnesen 海洋画 风景 天地 东南亚 油画 维基共享资源 《湄公河上的“安南号”》是维尔赫尔姆·阿内森约1900年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“湄公河上的“安南号””为题，属于越南的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "the steamer annam on the mekong near saigon 1900 1900 southeast asia vilhelm arnesen marine painting landscape heaven and earth southeast asia oil painting wikimedia commons 1900, southeast asia. 维尔赫尔姆·阿内森; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:vilhelm arnesen - dampskibet annam på mekongfloden ved saigon - 1900.png. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-2df8ce6f": ["男孩肖像 portrait of a boy, by george benjamin luks portrait of a boy 1900 1900 跨地域 george benjamin luks 垃圾箱画派 面孔 人间 跨地域 油画 维基共享资源 《男孩肖像》是乔治·本杰明·卢克斯约1900年的垃圾箱画派作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“男孩肖像”为题，属于美国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "portrait of a boy 1900 1900 cross-regional george benjamin luks ashcan school faces human world cross-regional oil painting wikimedia commons 1900, cross-regional. 乔治·本杰明·卢克斯; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:portrait of a boy, by george benjamin luks.png. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-256d170f": ["葡萄静物 edith white - still life with grapes (c. 1900) still life with grapes 1900 1900 跨地域 edith white (american, 1855-1946) 美国静物画 痕迹 技艺 跨地域 油画 维基共享资源 《葡萄静物》是伊迪丝·怀特约1900年的美国静物画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“葡萄静物”为题，属于美国的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "still life with grapes 1900 1900 cross-regional edith white (american, 1855-1946) american still life traces craft cross-regional oil painting wikimedia commons 1900, cross-regional. 伊迪丝·怀特; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:edith white still life with grapes 1900.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-91d0ab3b": ["锡兰海域 vilhelm arnesen - under ceylon - 1900 under ceylon 1900 1900 南亚 vilhelm arnesen 海洋画 风景 天地 南亚 油画 维基共享资源 《锡兰海域》是维尔赫尔姆·阿内森约1900年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“锡兰海域”为题，属于锡兰的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "under ceylon 1900 1900 south asia vilhelm arnesen marine painting landscape heaven and earth south asia oil painting wikimedia commons 1900, south asia. 维尔赫尔姆·阿内森; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:vilhelm arnesen - under ceylon - 1900.png. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "cezanne-mont-sainte-victoire-1904": ["《圣维克多山》 1904 1902–1904 欧洲 保罗·塞尚 后印象主义 风景 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 圣维克多山是塞尚晚年反复描绘的主题。这座山被分解成平行的笔触——赭色、灰绿色、浅蓝色——像石块一样，也像呼吸一样；前景的树木和田野没有清晰的边界，只有推进和后退的色块。天空和山共享同一色调尺度；空间不是通过透视构建的，而是通过色彩的温度和笔触的方向来塑造的。\n\n塞尚同一个景色画了几十次，不是为了记录风景，而是为了找到结构。他把绘画从“看到的东西”转向“视觉如何被组织”，这是立体主义将要采纳的一步。", "mont sainte-victoire 1904 1902–1904 europe 保罗·塞尚 post-impressionism landscape heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons mont sainte-victoire was a motif cézanne returned to again and again in his late years. the mountain is broken into parallel strokes — ochre, grey-green, pale blue — like masonry and like breathing; trees and fields in the foreground have no clear edges, only blocks of colour advancing and receding. sky and mountain share one scale of tones; space is built not by perspective but by temperature of colour and direction of stroke.\n\ncézanne painted the same view dozens of times, not to record landscape but to find structure. he moved painting from \"what is seen\" to \"how seeing is organised,\" a step that cubism would take up."], "redon-vase-flowers-1905": ["《瓶花》 vase of flowers 1905 c. 1905 法国 巴黎 奥迪隆·雷东 象征主义 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 油画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1905年前后，雷东把花瓶放在画面中央，花瓣的边缘几乎融进背景；象征主义把可见的花当成不可见情绪的外壳。", "vase of flowers 1905 c. 1905 paris, france 奥迪隆·雷东 symbolism traces craft europe oil painting cleveland museum of art c. 1905, europe. 奥迪隆·雷东; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1935.233. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "klimt-the-kiss-1908": ["《吻》 1908 1907–1908 欧洲 古斯塔夫·克里姆特 新艺术运动 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面，金箔） 维基共享资源 《吻》展示了两个人物跪在花草繁茂的草地边缘：男人俯身靠向女人，她的脸朝上，闭着眼睛。他们的身体被一件巨大的金色斗篷包裹，斗篷上覆盖着圆形、矩形和眼睛形状；男人的衣服是黑白条纹的，女人的衣服则点缀着彩色圆点。背景是闪烁的金色场面，既像马赛克又像夜空。\n\n克里姆特将维也纳分离派的装饰推到极限：爱不仅是叙事，而是一种被包围的存在状态。金箔让画作减轻了重量，并将这对情侣从现实中提升到永恒的图案中。", "the kiss 1908 1907–1908 europe 古斯塔夫·克里姆特 art nouveau / vienna secession faces human world europe oil on canvas with gold leaf wikimedia commons the kiss shows two figures kneeling at the edge of a flower meadow: the man bends over the woman, her face tilted up, eyes closed. their bodies are wrapped in a vast gold cloak covered with circles, rectangles and eye-like shapes; his garment is striped black and white, hers patterned with coloured dots. the background is a shimmering gold field, mosaic and night sky at once.\n\nklimt pushes vienna secession ornament to its limit: love is not a narrative but a state of being enclosed. gold leaf removes weight from the picture and lifts the couple out of reality into an eternal pattern."], "kamisaka-chrysanthemum-boy-1909": ["《百世界之花：菊童》 flowers of a hundred worlds (momoyogusa): chrysanthemum boy (kikujidō) 1909 1909 日本 京都 神坂雪佳 日本画 痕迹 技艺 东亚 素描 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 神坂雪佳为《百世界之花》画的菊童，线条和图案几乎同等重要；这是1909年的设计性绘画。", "flowers of a hundred worlds (momoyogusa): chrysanthemum boy (kikujidō) 1909 1909 日本 京都 神坂雪佳 nihonga traces craft east asia drawing cleveland museum of art 1909, east asia. 神坂雪佳; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1989.85.20. this is a drawing."], "kirchner-wrestlers-circus-1909": ["《马戏团里的摔跤手》 wrestlers in a circus 1909 1909 德国 柏林 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳 表现主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1909，德国 柏林。恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳的绘画，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。画面以博物馆公布的开放数据为准，人物、衣饰与光线都保留在作品自身的尺度里。", "wrestlers in a circus 1909 1909 berlin, germany 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳 expressionism faces human world europe oil on canvas cleveland museum of art 1909, europe. 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1966.49. this is a painting (oil on canvas)."], "posada-calavera-catrina-1910": ["《卡特里娜骷髅头》 calavera de la catrina (skull of the female dandy) 1910 c. 1910 墨西哥 墨西哥城 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达 墨西哥版画 灾变 世事 中南美 版画 维基共享资源 卡特里娜戴着一顶夸张的帽子，骷髅的脸被画成盛装女子的脸；死亡在这里被化装成社会身份。", "calavera de la catrina (skull of the female dandy) 1910 c. 1910 墨西哥 墨西哥城 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达 mexican printmaking disaster world affairs latin america print wikimedia commons c. 1910, latin america. 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. posada2.catrina.jpeg. this is a print."], "posada-jesus-negrete-1910": ["《赫苏斯·内格雷特（“圣胡利娅之虎”）的轰动阴谋》 the very sensational plot of jesús negrete, a.k.a. the tiger of santa julia 1910 c. 1910 墨西哥 墨西哥城 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达 墨西哥版画 灾变 世事 中南美 版画 维基共享资源 波萨达把一桩刑事案件画成大众印刷品：人物、动作和标题一起制造“轰动”，新闻与图像在这里没有分界。", "the very sensational plot of jesús negrete, a.k.a. the tiger of santa julia 1910 c. 1910 墨西哥 墨西哥城 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达 mexican printmaking disaster world affairs latin america print wikimedia commons c. 1910, latin america. 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. josé guadalupe posada - the very sensational plot of jesús negrete, a.k.a., the tiger of santa julia - google art project.jpg. this is a print."], "posada-frivolous-frog-1910": ["《轻浮的青蛙》 the frivolous frog 1910 before 1913 墨西哥 墨西哥城 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达 墨西哥版画 面孔 人间 中南美 版画 维基共享资源 波萨达的木刻把青蛙画成穿礼服的角色；动物、衣冠和人的姿态被压进同一条黑白轮廓。", "the frivolous frog 1910 before 1913 墨西哥 墨西哥城 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达 mexican printmaking faces human world latin america print wikimedia commons before 1913, latin america. 何塞·瓜达卢佩·波萨达; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. the frivolous frog by josé guadalupe posada, woodcut, honolulu museum of art.jpg. this is a print."], "delaunay-eiffel-tower-1911": ["《埃菲尔铁塔》 1911 1911 欧洲 罗贝尔·德劳内 奥费主义 街巷 天地 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 德拉纳伊把埃菲尔铁塔变成了一根旋转的彩色柱子。铁质结构被分解成红棕色、橙色和灰蓝色的面；云层以环形爆开，周围的公寓楼向铁塔倾斜。他没有使用立体主义的单色分析；颜色本身就创造了空间——暖色面向前推进，冷色面后退，铁质格子在其中若隐若现。\n\n1911年的巴黎是一个充满飞机、海报、地铁和电灯的城市。这幅画让“同时性”变成了视觉体验：你无法一次看到整座铁塔，只能同时感受到它的几个面。", "eiffel tower (tour eiffel) 1911 1911 europe 罗贝尔·德劳内 orphism streets heaven and earth europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons delaunay turns the eiffel tower into a rotating column of colour. the iron structure is broken into red-brown, orange and grey-blue facets; clouds burst in rings, and the surrounding apartment blocks tilt toward the tower. he does not use the monochrome analysis of cubism; colour itself creates space — warm planes advance, cool planes recede, and the iron lattice appears and disappears between them.\n\nparis in 1911 was a city of aeroplanes, posters, the metro and electric light. the painting turns 'simultaneity' into visual experience: you cannot see the tower all at once, only feel several of its faces at the same time."], "schiele-self-portrait-1912": ["《与中国灯笼花自画像》 1912 1912 欧洲 埃贡·席勒 表现主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（木板） 维基共享资源 《带中国灯笼植物的自画像》展示了席勒本人：瘦削的身体，肩膀耸起，头微微倾斜，眼睛睁大；右手扭在胸前，手指像小树枝。右侧挂着一株中国灯笼植物，橙色的花萼像小灯笼。背景是空白的，几乎没有空间感。\n\n席勒将自画像变成了一种生理和心理的展露：身体不舒适，表情警觉，就像被看见的动物。那紧绷的线条是维也纳表现主义最锐利的边缘。", "self-portrait with chinese lantern plant 1912 1912 europe 埃贡·席勒 expressionism faces human world europe oil on wood wikimedia commons self-portrait with chinese lantern plant shows schiele himself: thin body, shoulders raised, head tilted, eyes wide; his right hand twisted across his chest, fingers like twigs. at the right hangs a chinese lantern plant, its orange calyces like small lamps. the background is blank, with almost no space.\n\nschiele makes the self-portrait a physiological and psychological exposure: the body uncomfortable, the expression alert, like an animal that has been seen. that taut line is the sharpest edge of viennese expressionism."], "gris-portrait-of-picasso-1912": ["《毕加索肖像》 1912 1912 欧洲 胡安·格里斯 立体主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 1912年，胡安·格里斯画了他朋友圈里最著名的肖像：毕加索。面部被切成不同的面，从正面、侧面和顶部同时呈现；灰蓝色、赭色和冷白色被压成几乎单色的和弦。格里斯不仅仅是在“打破”毕加索；他是以几何方式重建表情——眼睛像两道斜坡，鼻子是折叠的线条，手像一张纸。\n\n背景中的对角线与衣领的三角形相互交错，把肖像变成了建筑。这标志着分析立体主义从拆解物体转向构建画面，同时格里斯也不再仅仅是追随者。", "portrait of pablo picasso 1912 1912 europe 胡安·格里斯 cubism faces human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons in 1912 juan gris painted the most famous portrait of his circle: picasso. the face is cut into facets, front, side and top view appearing at once; grey-blue, ochre and cool white are pressed into an almost monochrome chord. gris does not simply 'break' picasso; he rebuilds the expression geometrically — eyes as two slopes, the nose a folded line, the hand a sheet of paper.\n\ndiagonals in the background interlock with the triangles of the collar, turning the portrait into architecture. it marks analytical cubism moving from dismantling objects to constructing a picture, and gris becoming more than a follower."], "yoshimura-howling-wolf-1912": ["《深山啸狼》 howling wolf in a deep mountain valley 1912 1912 日本 吉村凤龙 日本画 风景 天地 东亚 绘画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1912年的绢本挂轴，狼站在雪谷里抬头长啸；日本画把动物的动势压进留白和雾。", "howling wolf in a deep mountain valley 1912 1912 日本 吉村凤龙 nihonga landscape heaven and earth east asia painting cleveland museum of art 1912, east asia. 吉村凤龙; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1989.474. this is a painting."], "kandinsky-composition-vii-1913": ["《构成第七号》 1913 1913 欧洲 瓦西里·康定斯基 抽象艺术 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 《构图 vii》是康定斯基抽象画的巅峰之作。画中没有可辨认的物体，只有巨大的色块、弧线、黑色线条和密集的旋转笔触；中心像一次爆炸，边缘则像碎片被吸引进来。颜色相互碰撞；红、蓝、黄、绿在同一空间中争论又和解。\n\n康定斯基把绘画比作音乐：不是描述世界，而是直接作用于感情。他为这幅画做了数十幅研究，最终呈现为一次视觉盛宴，其中末日与重生同时发生。", "composition vii 1913 1913 europe 瓦西里·康定斯基 abstract art / der blaue reiter traces craft europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons composition vii is the summit of kandinsky's abstract painting. there are no recognisable objects, only enormous colour masses, arcs, black lines and dense strokes in rotation; the centre reads as an explosion, the edges as fragments being drawn in. colours push against one another; red, blue, yellow and green argue and reconcile in the same space.\n\nkandinsky compared painting to music: not describing the world but acting directly on feeling. he made dozens of studies for this picture, and what remains is a visual event in which apocalypse and rebirth happen at once."], "kirchner-street-berlin-1913": ["《柏林街景》 1913 1913 欧洲 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳 表现主义 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 柏林街头展示了两条交叉的城市街道。前景中两位穿着时尚黑色衣服、戴着夸张帽子的女性，她们的脸被简化为尖锐、几乎像面具的三角形；街道被切成对角线，行人像风中纸片般弯曲。\n\n基尔希纳将城市的刺激、速度和不安转化为视觉张力：酸粉色、绿色和黑色，短促而尖锐的笔触。表现主义并不在意街道是否正确；它在意的是城市在身体中产生的震动。", "street, berlin 1913 1913 europe 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳 expressionism streets human world europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons street, berlin shows two intersecting city streets. in the foreground two women in fashionable black clothes and exaggerated hats, their faces reduced to sharp, almost mask-like triangles; the street is cut into diagonals, pedestrians bent like paper figures in wind.\n\nkirchner turns urban stimulus, speed and unease into visual tension: acid pink, green and black, short and sharp strokes. expressionism does not care whether the street is correct; it cares about the vibration the city produces in the body."], "malevich-black-square-1915": ["《黑方块》 1915 1915 欧洲 卡济米尔·马列维奇 至上主义 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 油画（亚麻布） 维基共享资源 《黑方块》并不是描绘一个具体的物体，而是一种姿态：一个黑色的四边形在白色的背景上，边缘不完全笔直，笔触隐约可见。马列维奇在1915年的“0.10”展览中把它挂在角落里，就像一尊圣像一样，让观众在原本应有神圣画像的位置上看到“空白”。它宣告了至上主义的诞生：绘画不再模仿自然或讲述故事，而是回归最基本的形状和颜色。黑方块不是终点，而是一扇门——在它那端，是白色、空白的画布。", "black square 1915 1915 europe 卡济米尔·马列维奇 suprematism traces craft europe oil on linen wikimedia commons black square does not depict an object but a gesture: a black quadrilateral on a white ground, its edges not quite straight, the brushwork faintly visible. malevich hung it in the corner of the 1915 \"0.10\" exhibition like an icon, so that viewers encountered \"nothing\" where a holy image would normally stand.\n\nit announced suprematism: painting no longer imitates nature or tells stories but returns to the elementary form and colour. the black square is not an end but a door — beyond it lie the white, empty canvases."], "schiele-portrait-child-1916": ["《儿童肖像（安东·佩施卡之子）》 portrait of a child (anton peschka jr.) 1916 1916 奥地利 维也纳 埃贡·席勒 表现主义 面孔 人间 欧洲 素描（水粉、水彩、石墨） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1916，奥地利 维也纳。埃贡·席勒的素描，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件纸本素描，笔触和留白比完成度更直接。", "portrait of a child (anton peschka jr.) 1916 1916 奥地利 维也纳 埃贡·席勒 expressionism faces human world europe 素描（水粉、水彩、石墨） cleveland museum of art 1916, europe. 埃贡·席勒; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1964.285. this is a drawing (素描（水粉、水彩、石墨）)."], "wenning-rhodes-memorial-1916": ["《罗得斯纪念堂》 rhodes memorial 1916 1916 南非 开普敦 皮特·温宁 南非风景画 风景 天地 撒哈拉以南非洲 油画 维基共享资源 温宁画的是开普敦桌山下的罗得斯纪念堂；建筑被山体压住，石阶和树影把视线一级级带上去。", "rhodes memorial 1916 1916 南非 开普敦 皮特·温宁 south african landscape landscape heaven and earth sub-saharan africa oil painting wikimedia commons 1916, sub-saharan africa. 皮特·温宁; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. pieter wenning - rhodes memorial - google art project.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "kirchner-mountain-landscape-1918": ["《冷杉山景》 mountain landscape with fir trees 1918 1918/19 瑞士 达沃斯 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳 表现主义 风景 天地 欧洲 素描（石墨、毛笔、墨） 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 1918/19，瑞士 达沃斯。恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳的素描，今藏克利夫兰艺术博物馆。这是一件纸本素描，笔触和留白比完成度更直接。", "mountain landscape with fir trees 1918 1918/19 瑞士 达沃斯 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳 expressionism landscape heaven and earth europe 素描（石墨、毛笔、墨） cleveland museum of art 1918/19, europe. 恩斯特·路德维希·基尔希纳; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1963.86. this is a drawing (素描（石墨、毛笔、墨）)."], "auto-f2dad429": ["柏林夜间街景 lesser ury - nächtliche strassenszene, berlin (1920) night street scene, berlin 1920 1920 欧洲 lesser ury 印象主义 街巷 人间 欧洲 油画 维基共享资源 《柏林夜间街景》是莱塞·乌里约1920年的印象主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“柏林夜间街景”为题，属于柏林的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "night street scene, berlin 1920 1920 europe lesser ury impressionism streets human world europe oil painting wikimedia commons 1920, europe. 莱塞·乌里; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:lesser ury - nächtliche strassenszene, berlin (1920).jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-505fc4ea": ["老人肖像 ivan žabota - portret starca portrait of an old man 1920 1920 跨地域 ivan žabota 现实主义 面孔 人间 跨地域 油画 维基共享资源 《老人肖像》是伊万·扎博塔约1920年的现实主义作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“老人肖像”为题，属于斯拉夫的油画传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "portrait of an old man 1920 1920 cross-regional ivan žabota realism faces human world cross-regional oil painting wikimedia commons 1920, cross-regional. 伊万·扎博塔; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:ivan žabota - portret starca.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "auto-c6739d13": ["柯克卡迪港的渔船 kirkcaldy fishing boat in harbour kirkcaldy fishing boat in harbour 1925 1925 欧洲 john hamilton glass 海洋画 劳作 人间 欧洲 水彩 维基共享资源 《柯克卡迪港的渔船》是约翰·汉密尔顿·格拉斯约1925年的海洋画作品，现藏信息待考。画面以“柯克卡迪港的渔船”为题，属于苏格兰的水彩传统，可作为同时代绘画的参照。", "kirkcaldy fishing boat in harbour 1925 1925 europe john hamilton glass marine painting work human world europe watercolour wikimedia commons 1925, europe. 约翰·汉密尔顿·格拉斯; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. file:kirkcaldy fishing boat in harbour.jpg. this is a painting (watercolour)."], "mondrian-composition-red-yellow-blue-1927": ["《红、黄、蓝构成》 composition with red, yellow, and blue 1927 1927 法国 巴黎 皮特·蒙德里安 风格派 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 油画 克利夫兰艺术博物馆 黑色线把画面切成不等大的矩形，红黄蓝只占少数面积；蒙德里安用最少的颜色测试平衡。", "composition with red, yellow, and blue 1927 1927 paris, france 皮特·蒙德里安 de stijl traces craft europe oil painting cleveland museum of art 1927, europe. 皮特·蒙德里安; source: cleveland museum of art, catalog no. 1967.215. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "xu-beihong-tianheng-five-hundred-1930": ["《田横五百士》 tianheng and his five hundred followers 1930 1930 中国 南京 徐悲鸿 中国现代油画 战火 世事 中国 油画 维基共享资源 1930年，徐悲鸿把田横与五百士的故事画成油画；人物群像在画面右侧排开，海与天把决绝留在空白里。", "tianheng and his five hundred followers 1930 1930 中国 南京 徐悲鸿 chinese modern oil painting war world affairs china oil painting wikimedia commons 1930, china. 徐悲鸿; source: wikimedia commons, catalog no. xu beihong painting tianheng's five hundreds heroes.jpg. this is a painting (oil painting)."], "mondrian-composition-red-blue-yellow-1930": ["《红、蓝、黄构图》 1930 1930 欧洲 皮特·蒙德里安 风格派 痕迹 技艺 欧洲 油画（布面） 维基共享资源 蒙德里安的《红、蓝、黄构图》只包含黑色线条、白色背景和三个基础色平面。一个大红色矩形占据主导位置；蓝色位于左下角，一个小黄位于右下角；黑色线条不对称移动，这里厚、那里细，追求平衡而不是形成网格。\n\n蒙德里安称这种关系为新造型主义：水平和垂直代表宇宙的两种基本力量，原色代表纯净能量，白色代表空间。没有故事，但画作需要长时间凝视：每次注意力的转移，颜色的重量都会改变。", "composition ii in red, blue and yellow 1930 1930 europe 皮特·蒙德里安 de stijl / neo-plasticism traces craft europe oil on canvas wikimedia commons mondrian's *composition with red, blue and yellow* contains only black lines, white ground and three primary planes. a large red rectangle dominates; blue sits at lower left, a small yellow at lower right; the black lines move asymmetrically, thicker here, thinner there, seeking balance rather than executing a grid.\n\nmondrian called this relationship neo-plasticism: horizontal and vertical stand for the two basic forces of the universe, primary colours for pure energy, white for space. there is no story, yet the painting asks for prolonged looking: with every shift of attention, the weight of the colours changes."], "wood-american-gothic-1930": ["《美国哥特式》 1930 1930 北美 格兰特·伍德 美国地方主义 面孔 人间 北美 油画（纤维板） 维基共享资源 《美国哥特式》展示了一位父亲和女儿站在爱荷华州一栋白色木屋前。男人穿着黑色外套，戴着眼镜，手里拿着一把干草叉；女人稍微站在他身后，围裙上有图案，头发梳得很紧。房子的尖形窗户是木匠哥特式的，看起来像一座小教堂。\n\n格兰特·伍德把中西部的本地人物变成了几乎宗教般的肖像：严肃、封闭，又带着一种防御性的尊严。这幅画成了美国画作里最容易被误解的作品——有人看到坚忍不拔，有人看到压抑，两种解读都成立。", "american gothic 1930 1930 north america 格兰特·伍德 american regionalism faces human world north america oil on beaverboard wikimedia commons american gothic shows a father and daughter standing before a white timber house in iowa. the man wears a black coat and glasses, a pitchfork in his hand; the woman stands slightly behind him, her apron patterned, her hair pulled tight. the pointed window of the house is carpenter gothic, like a small church.\n\ngrant wood turns a midwestern local type into an almost religious portrait: severe, closed, with a defensive dignity. it became the most misread of american paintings — some see endurance, others repression, and both readings hold."]}, "stories": {}};
